{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington","id":1031175,"title":"The Women's March on Washington","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-13T08:42:23-08:00","id":1031175,"title":"The Women's March on Washington","content":"Since the topic of Feminism, what it looks like and what it stands for, came up yesterday, this seems particularly relevant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.slate.com/blogs/xx_factor/2017/01/12/the_women_s_march_on_washington_has_released_its_platform_and_it_is_unapologetically.html\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://compote.slate.com/images/f14c3503-98dd-4a59-8fa0-5e09e65dca3e.jpg?width=1560\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.slate.com/blogs/xx_factor/2017/01/12/the_women_s_march_on_washington_has_released_its_platform_and_it_is_unapologetically.html\" target=\"_blank\"> The Women&rsquo;s March on Washington Has Released an Unapologetically Progressive Platform </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.slate.com/blogs/xx_factor/2017/01/12/the_women_s_march_on_washington_has_released_its_platform_and_it_is_unapologetically.html\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.slate.com/blogs/xx_factor/2017/01/12/the_women_s_march_on_washington_has_released_its_platform_and_it_is_unapologetically.html </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> The Women&rsquo;s March on Washington has released its official policy platform, a far-reaching four-page statement that takes clear stances on reproductive... </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T08:59:18-08:00","id":1031183,"title":"","content":"Ugh. Forum crashed on me mid-post. So anyway this is just the tip of the iceberg of what I see and think of when I think of Feminism. For more details on the platform itself, the Womens' March webpage has the details. <a href=\"https://www.womensmarch.com/principles\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.womensmarch.com/principles</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T09:39:22-08:00","id":1031217,"title":"","content":"Everything about this is amazing, and I wish I was able to attend (I live nearby, but have to be in a wedding in Texas that weekend).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T10:03:05-08:00","id":1031224,"title":"","content":"Interesting. Seems like theres been some conflict with the organization of the march. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://mobile.nytimes.com/2017/01/09/us/womens-march-on-washington-opens-contentious-dialogues-about-race.html?_r=1&amp;referer=http://www.slate.com/blogs/xx_factor/2017/01/12/the_women_s_march_on_washington_has_released_its_platform_and_it_is_unapologetically.html\" target=\"_blank\">https://mobile.nytimes.com/2017/01/0...getically.html</a><br /> <br /> I hope it turns out well for everyone involved, overall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T10:16:43-08:00","id":1031228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1031224#post1031224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting. Seems like theres been some conflict with the organization of the march.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://mobile.nytimes.com/2017/01/09/us/womens-march-on-washington-opens-contentious-dialogues-about-race.html?_r=1&amp;referer=http://www.slate.com/blogs/xx_factor/2017/01/12/the_women_s_march_on_washington_has_released_its_platform_and_it_is_unapologetically.html\" target=\"_blank\">https://mobile.nytimes.com/2017/01/0...getically.html</a><br /> <br /> I hope it turns out well for everyone involved, overall.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unsurprising, and a little tragic. Ultimately I think making the march about a broader progressive platform is a good thing, but as a white, mostly-straight, cis male who's very aware of his privileges and advantages it can get irritating to hear &quot;Check your privilege&quot; over and over again. Of course, my coping mechanism is to remember that being mildly irritated is a minor quibble in comparison to most people, so I grin and bear it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T10:16:45-08:00","id":1031229,"title":"","content":"&quot;All women should be paid equitably, with access to affordable childcare, sick days, healthcare, paid family leave, and healthy work environments.&quot;<br /> <br /> And what about men?<br /> <br /> I have no problem protesting Trump, although I doubt Trump, or the Republican held Senate and Congress will care honestly. A Independents March of Swing voters in key states, that he might care about, but a group of female (or even male ) democracts, their votes aren't on the table so why would Trump give two fucks about it. A best they'll earn an insulting tweet from the President. <br /> <br /> If they want to protect abortion rights, focus on turning the democracts into a party of asskicking, focused on Trump vulnerable points, give independants and open minded Republicans someone worth voting for, win during the midterm elections.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 01-13-2017, 01:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T10:18:22-08:00","id":1031231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1031229#post1031229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;All women should be paid equitably, with access to affordable childcare, sick days, healthcare, paid family leave, and healthy work environments.&quot;<br /> <br /> And what about men?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's funny how if they said &quot;All men should be etc.., etc...&quot; then nobody would bat an eye because &quot;Men&quot; is the presumed default pronoun, but when you use &quot;women&quot; people like you come in and start bitching about exclusive language.<br /> <br /> Wait, not funny. That other thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T10:45:31-08:00","id":1031241,"title":"","content":"It's also the other not-funny thing when someone responds to, &quot;women should get paid the same as men, and a bunch of workplace demands that befit everyone&quot; with, &quot;what about the men?&quot; as if paying women the same as men, and giving everyone better benefits somehow changes anything negatively for men.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T10:48:06-08:00","id":1031243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1031241#post1031241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's also the other not-funny thing when someone responds to, &quot;women should get paid the same as men, and a bunch of workplace demands that befit everyone&quot; with, &quot;what about the men?&quot; as if paying women the same as men, and giving everyone better benefits somehow changes anything negatively for men.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, if you're somehow possessed of the idiotic notion that women already have advantages that men don't have, it looks like men are getting the short end of the stick when women catch up. I can't think of anybody off hand who would hold such ignorant views, but I know they're out there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T10:56:03-08:00","id":1031247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1031229#post1031229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&amp;quot;All women should be paid equitably, with access to affordable childcare, sick days, healthcare, paid family leave, and healthy work environments.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> And what about men?</div> </div> </div> </div>*winces*<br /> <br /> I'm sorry, man. But that's a question that bad actors have really turned into a poison pill.<br /> <br /> Maybe think of it like this? If women get reliable access to those benefits, there's less reason for men to be denied those benefits, too. And that helps us all, right? So I think that's extra reason to support them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T11:13:11-08:00","id":1031256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1031228#post1031228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unsurprising, and a little tragic. Ultimately I think making the march about a broader progressive platform is a good thing, but as a white, mostly-straight, cis male who's very aware of his privileges and advantages it can get irritating to hear &amp;quot;Check your privilege&amp;quot; over and over again. Of course, my coping mechanism is to remember that being mildly irritated is a minor quibble in comparison to most people, so I grin and bear it.</div> </div> </div> </div>This really depends on how &quot;check your privilege&quot; is being used. It's a GREAT tool to make you reevaluate your position on something so you can better find common ground and empathize or sympathize with other people. <br /> <br /> Unfortunately, it's also used as a weapon to guilt and shame people, to express that they're not allowed to speak, or partake of the discussion that they are explicitly a part of and that their place is to be lectured at.<br /> <br /> Used carefully and compassionately, it's very useful to help build bridges. Used carelessly and abusively, it'll burn any bridges being built down to their foundation. <br /> <br /> I pay attention to the context of it, because well... I'm listening.<br /> <br /> Really do hope this March turns out well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T11:20:23-08:00","id":1031262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1031229#post1031229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;All women should be paid equitably, with access to affordable childcare, sick days, healthcare, paid family leave, and healthy work environments.&quot;<br /> <br /> And what about men?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Trump has hit a sore spot with some of his statements involving woman. Since women are doing the heavy lifting for this March, we are mobilizing for issues that are important to us. <br /> <br /> I personally have no objections to a Men's Right March on Washington. But please don't tear down someone else's work because it doesn't include things that are important to you. If you wish to get involved, stop arguing with people on the internet and join some organizations. If a Male Right's group wants to put in the work to organize a march, they are welcome to do so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T12:30:17-08:00","id":1031288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1031256#post1031256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Used carefully and compassionately, it's very useful to help build bridges. Used carelessly and abusively, it'll burn any bridges being built down to their foundation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have found that while the ideal of &quot;check your privilege&quot; is meant as a way to helpfully suggest someone reconsider a situation in a different light, it's just as often used as a way to reject or dismiss someone by essentially saying that they are out of touch and that their views and opinions should not be considered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T12:54:14-08:00","id":1031293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1031288#post1031288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have found that while the ideal of &quot;check your privilege&quot; is meant as a way to helpfully suggest someone reconsider a situation in a different light, it's just as often used as a way to reject or dismiss someone by essentially saying that they are out of touch and that their views and opinions should not be considered.</div> </div> </div> </div>I personally haven't seen it used that way, though I have seen it used as &quot;Oh no, not this topic again...&quot;, which can be easily misinterpreted that way by the privileged.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T12:59:46-08:00","id":1031295,"title":"","content":"Something that I think is often elided in discussions about privilege is that privilege contains a contextual dimension. It is experienced in different ways by different people in different situations. There isn't a neat binary division between the privileged and the unprivileged. That doesn't mean that invoking privilege is necessarily unproductive. On the contrary, the umbrage that most people feel at having their perceived privilege challenged is a pretty good indicator that we all acknowledge privilege is a bad thing. Nobody wants to be privileged, and certainly nobody wants to feel like their struggles, experiences, or work are somehow diminished by it. Using privilege as a rhetorical tool should be the beginning of a conversation, but unfortunately it often marks the end of meaningful dialogue, either because someone is using it to invalidate the perspective of another or because someone rejects the validity of privilege as an argument and ceases to deal in good faith thereafter. <br /> <br /> Privilege is real, but we talk about it poorly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T13:21:51-08:00","id":1031302,"title":"","content":"Normally I don't go after such an easy target and its low-hanging fruit, but I missed the Misogynist's Rights Advocacy/Movement thread.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1031229#post1031229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;All women should be paid equitably, with access to affordable childcare, sick days, healthcare, paid family leave, and healthy work environments.&quot;<br /> <br /> And what about men?</div> </div> </div> </div>Really tho, why are you against women being paid equitably? I mean, you are aware that across the board, men out-earn women, even when they're both in similar positions. You can't be blind to that. You just can't. So why do you have to throw in &quot;but wut 'bout the MENSES?!?&quot;<br /> <br /> When minority groups protest their own unfair treatment, do you shout &quot;but what about whites&quot;?<br /> When LGBTQ groups protest their mistreatment, do you shout out &quot;but what about straights&quot;?<br /> When groups protest the mistreatment of the mentally ill, do you shout out &quot;but what about the sane&quot;?<br /> When groups advocate for the homeless, do you shout out &quot;but what about those with a home&quot;?<br /> <br /> And if your answer is no to all of those and those look like insane stances to make to you, why do you think it's better when you say &quot;but what about men&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T13:50:26-08:00","id":1031314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1031231#post1031231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's funny how if they said &quot;All men should be etc.., etc...&quot; then nobody would bat an eye because &quot;Men&quot; is the presumed default pronoun, but when you use &quot;women&quot; people like you come in and start bitching about exclusive language.<br /> <br /> Wait, not funny. That other thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, the words man, men, mankind, etc have (for like, a thousand years, if not longer) been used in the English language as a way to identify all people, of every race, sex, gender, etc. The word women simply does not have that kind of historical precedent behind. I think it's entirely reasonable that when people begin using words to mean new ideas that they generally haven't meant in the past, for there to be some level of confusion and misunderstanding.<br /> <br /> And to be clear there's nothing wrong with using the world &quot;women&quot; to refer to both men and women or indeed changing any other word to mean whatever you want (if there's not a word in English for what you want, just make one up or appropriate an old one or take one from another language) but at the same time you probably shouldn't get too snarky at people who don't realize that you've decided to change what a word means from its traditional definition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T14:05:25-08:00","id":1031322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1031314#post1031314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be fair, the words man, men, mankind, etc have (for like, a thousand years, if not longer) been used in the English language as a way to identify all people, of every race, sex, gender, etc. The word women simply does not have that kind of historical precedent behind. I think it's entirely reasonable that when people begin using words to mean new ideas that they generally haven't meant in the past, for there to be some level of confusion and misunderstanding.<br /> <br /> And to be clear there's nothing wrong with using the world &amp;quot;women&amp;quot; to refer to both men and women or indeed changing any other word to mean whatever you want (if there's not a word in English for what you want, just make one up or appropriate an old one or take one from another language) but at the same time you probably shouldn't get too snarky at people who don't realize that you've decided to change what a word means from its traditional definition.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always think that semantics is incredibly important, because semantics is all about the meaning of the words we use. And if we're trying to have a conversation with words we think mean different things to each other, it becomes incredibly difficult to have it be either meaningful or productive. <br /> <br /> Ultimately, words are arbitrary. They're just a noise that we assign an idea to. Establishing a fundamental understanding is crucial to making progress.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T14:22:46-08:00","id":1031326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1031314#post1031314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, the words man, men, mankind, etc have (for like, a thousand years, if not longer) been used in the English language as a way to identify all people, of every race, sex, gender, etc. The word women simply does not have that kind of historical precedent behind.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure that was the whole point of calling out &quot;men&quot; as the presumed default.<br /> <br /> Though as a linguistic nitpick, while there are thousands of years of linguistic bias in this direction, it's not really that old in English. Proto-, Old, and even some Middle English maintained the Germanic words that kept these concepts separated. &quot;A male human,&quot; and, &quot;humans in general,&quot; were separate words in English until fairly recently (in linguistic scale of time anyway). The evolution of Modern English in many ways made the language more biased than the languages of its origin (though it is complicated by English dropping the concept of grammatical gender when the primary languages English draws from use the concept heavily) by combining multiple words and limiting the ability to express concepts without extra front loading of linguistic bias.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think it's entirely reasonable that when people begin using words to mean new ideas that they generally haven't meant in the past, for there to be some level of confusion and misunderstanding. </div> </div> </div>Who the hell is doing that?<br /> <br /> The point was that certain people hear, &quot;All men should get...&quot; and hear, &quot;All people should get,&quot; while hearing, &quot;All women should get...&quot; and hear, &quot;All women should get at the expense of men...&quot;<br /> <br /> It's pointing out how people will take the smallest semantic point to try to twist the conversation towards an artificially antagonistic view of the fight for women's rights issues by using inclusion of the word &quot;women&quot; to inherently mean an exclusion of men.<br /> <br /> It's not using &quot;women&quot; in a definition that not traditional.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T06:14:13-08:00","id":1031550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1031231#post1031231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's funny how if they said &amp;quot;All men should be etc.., etc...&amp;quot; then nobody would bat an eye because &amp;quot;Men&amp;quot; is the presumed default pronoun, but when you use &amp;quot;women&amp;quot; people like you come in and start bitching about exclusive language.<br /> <br /> Wait, not funny. That other thing.</div> </div> </div> </div> Actually in school I was taught that man was originally genderless, it refered to the whole species, but later became gendered when someone came up with woman (wool women), but I don't know if it's true or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T06:30:04-08:00","id":1031556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vysha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1031302#post1031302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Normally I don't go after such an easy target and its low-hanging fruit, but I missed the Misogynist's Rights Advocacy/Movement thread.<br /> <br /> Really tho, why are you against women being paid equitably? I mean, you are aware that across the board, men out-earn women, even when they're both in similar positions. You can't be blind to that. You just can't. So why do you have to throw in &amp;quot;but wut 'bout the MENSES?!?&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> When minority groups protest their own unfair treatment, do you shout &amp;quot;but what about whites&amp;quot;?<br /> When LGBTQ groups protest their mistreatment, do you shout out &amp;quot;but what about straights&amp;quot;?<br /> When groups protest the mistreatment of the mentally ill, do you shout out &amp;quot;but what about the sane&amp;quot;?<br /> When groups advocate for the homeless, do you shout out &amp;quot;but what about those with a home&amp;quot;?<br /> <br /> And if your answer is no to all of those and those look like insane stances to make to you, why do you think it's better when you say &amp;quot;but what about men&amp;quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/IE29WXXT17Q\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/IE29WXXT17Q\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/IE29WXXT17Q\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/IE29WXXT17Q </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I'm handing responding to your pushing of the wage gap to Shoeonhead, but there are countless refutation videos on YouTube that dispel that myth. <br /> <br /> But I will add paying women less for the same work as men is ILLEGAL just about everywhere in the West, so if you see it happening, don't protest get a lawyer and put forth a Lawsuit, the lawsuit will be far more effective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","