div> I take a look at later, I'm absolutely open to a more nausanced perspective on the issue. <br /> <br /> There was also a German experiment where they created a game with payouts that eliminated the possibility of gender biases, payouts we're based on choices and risks takes by the players and a wage gap emerged between the genders without any gender biases, it's was all automated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T14:44:46-08:00","id":1031824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vysha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1031816#post1031816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sorry, but I cannot control what you see. I can assure you it's not happening, but it's okay if you disagree. But could you please do me just one thing? Can you quote or point out anywhere that I judged the kink in question? For my part in resolving it, <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://computer.howstuffworks.com/what-is-doxxing.htm&amp;quot;]here</a> is what doxing is[/URL]. Nothing personal nor private was released.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;You also write fetishized rape porn (and of course much more than just rape, but no need to go into that) and say it doesn't reflect your values... &quot;<br /> <br /> This is you attacking the poster instead of the argument, specifically using an example of a kink, while also insinuating there's more awful salaciousness.<br /> <br /> And yes, actually, what you did was doxing. You deliberately released personal information about that user, that if another site they visit and likely personal sexual interests. Doxing isn't just phone numbers, home addresses or real names. Its about tying the pieces of information that are out there together. Just because you got it from googling doesn't mean it's not doxing.<br /> <br /> By the way, deciding to deliberately go after sexual information like that and bring it into this thread is pretty damn creepy of you. Would you have gone digging through sex sites to find out what interests Omegaphallic was into if you thought they were a woman?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T14:58:18-08:00","id":1031833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1031818#post1031818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I take a look at later, I'm absolutely open to a more nausanced perspective on the issue. <br /> <br /> There was also a German experiment where they created a game with payouts that eliminated the possibility of gender biases, payouts we're based on choices and risks takes by the players and a wage gap emerged between the genders without any gender biases, it's was all automated.</div> </div> </div> </div>The video I linked addresses that some, along with some of the supporting sources they list in the description of the video. From my understanding of the topic, women get a lot of the burden of raising families, which requires them to often find jobs that allow for flexible work hours or part time work and decisions like that do create a gap in wages, but it's an explainable gap. The video mentions that even when looking at same careers, same education and work experience, the gap shrinks a lot, but there still exists around a 4-8% wage difference between men and women which isn't explained. It could be that gap exists for similar reasons, but we don't know what they might be, and it could come down to simple discrimination.<br /> <br /> That's as simple as I can sum it up. It's interesting and presented pretty forwardly. I like how they acknowledge that there a lot of nuance to this issue. And it shows that solutions might not be as simple as raising women's wages, because that doesn't address issues of women being expected to put more time into raising families. That's more of a culture thing. Expecting men to do more for that could help with that, but in order for that to be reasonable, men need to not have the cultural expectation of being the &quot;bread winners&quot; of the family. I like the idea of men having more support from their workplaces to enable them to better take care of their families. For one benefit that brings to women, they have less demands on their time from family that lets them devote more attention to cultivating their careers, which should help them get higher wages. <br /> <br /> That make sense?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T15:00:23-08:00","id":1031834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vysha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1031797#post1031797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a gulf of differences between shaming someone for a kink and pointing out a repeated pattern of behavior. Rape fantasies alone? Ok, not something you see every day, but you do you. Rape fantasies while attacking women's groups and claiming their issues are all made-up propaganda? That's not a kink. Following it up with similar comments here and elsewhere about other minority activist groups? Still not a kink.<br /> <br /> <br /> No details about anyone's real life, identity, location or what have you have been mentioned, save by the individuals themselves. There's a gulf of difference between a Google search for readily available information and dropping their personal information.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'd like to correct you on something, I critize certain groups when they act bigoted against someone, such as men, but I've also critized fellow MRAs for slut shaming or other things, I critized Social Conservatives for a long time, Libertarians for being economically unrealistic, White Supremeists for tons of things, ect... <br /> <br /> And I stood up for a feminists when I felt it was just, when some fellow MRAs accused Lena Durham of being a pedophile, I defended her, pointing out that childhood experimentations are not pedaphilia. <br /> <br /> I have chided fellow MRAs for taking some jokes about men too seriously.<br /> <br /> I supported girls being in boyscouts and boys being in girl guides for that matter (when I was boy scout the only difference between the boy scout troop with girls that I was apart of and the one that didn't have girls that I joined later, was that I got more action in the boys only one).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T15:13:51-08:00","id":1031841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1031833#post1031833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The video I linked addresses that some, along with some of the supporting sources they list in the description of the video. From my understanding of the topic, women get a lot of the burden of raising families, which requires them to often find jobs that allow for flexible work hours or part time work and decisions like that do create a gap in wages, but it's an explainable gap. The video mentions that even when looking at same careers, same education and work experience, the gap shrinks a lot, but there still exists around a 4-8% wage difference between men and women which isn't explained. It could be that gap exists for similar reasons, but we don't know what they might be, and it could come down to simple discrimination.<br /> <br /> That's as simple as I can sum it up. It's interesting and presented pretty forwardly. I like how they acknowledge that there a lot of nuance to this issue. And it shows that solutions might not be as simple as raising women's wages, because that doesn't address issues of women being expected to put more time into raising families. That's more of a culture thing. Expecting men to do more for that could help with that, but in order for that to be reasonable, men need to not have the cultural expectation of being the &amp;quot;bread winners&amp;quot; of the family. I like the idea of men having more support from their workplaces to enable them to better take care of their families. For one benefit that brings to women, they have less demands on their time from family that lets them devote more attention to cultivating their careers, which should help them get higher wages. <br /> <br /> That make sense?</div> </div> </div> </div> For that to happen women need to be more willing to share parenting, it's win for everyone, Dads get more access to their kids, women get more time for their careers!!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T15:18:26-08:00","id":1031844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1031841#post1031841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For that to happen women need to be more willing to share parenting, it's win for everyone, Dads get more access to their kids, women get more time for their careers!!!</div> </div> </div> </div>There are women who support such for men. Don't get trapped into thinking a demographic is monolithic. That won't help anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T15:37:57-08:00","id":1031850,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>We are going to drop discussion of Kink or MRAs from the thread. Stick to focusing on Women's issues and the March here. There are threads elsewhere for Kink and for MRA stuff.</b></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/m