e everything else in life there were a lot of factors. But I'd be willing to bet my left arm that the Civil Rights movement wouldn't have been as successful if it didn't have the leaders who were able to convince regular Americans, and union leaders and politicians and everyone else to get on their side.<br /> <br /> And while the civil rights movement may not have started with leadership, leaders did quickly begin emerging - Rev. Martin Luther King Jr. began leading the Montgomery bus boycott from practically day one, a year later he was one of the leading figures of the Civil Rights movement, and within just 3 was leading major Sit-ins and was inspiring people across America.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying it's fair to expect another person like him to pop up in today's world, but there's no doubt that BLM has actively resisted every attempt that anyone has made at taking control of the movement, and I honestly don't that's really helped them very much in spreading their message to America in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T21:08:17-08:00","id":1032471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1032384#post1032384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <