035877#post1035877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pretty sure that's on the docket next after his bizarre meeting with the CIA and his disturbing comments about making sure to display the military prominently. It might never occur to him but today was a clear and resounding world wide declaration that I think folk like Omegaphallic's overstatements about why Orange Mussolini won are just that, overstatements.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> He won because of a) the last minute misleading info by the FBI (and the general confusion in the public over the conflation of &quot;emails&quot; - huge numbers of people thought/think that the stolen embarrassing, but not criminal, Clinton &amp; DNC emails were the ones on her private server and were stolen because of that issue, when actually the private server with classified info on it was never breached); and b) our arcane system that was designed to protect the electoral interest of slave owners from more diverse majorities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T17:30:18-08:00","id":1035904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1035871#post1035871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">God I hope we get a full twitter tirade about how the vastly larger opposition march than inaugural attendance is some kind of media conspiracy!</div> </div> </div> </div>Already done. Via Press Secretary, no less. First day on his job and already ignoring the worldwide march for women to say 'my party was bigger, everyone who says different is a liar.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T21:02:44-08:00","id":1035940,"title":"","content":"So great that so many got together, united for one common ideal. All across the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T10:07:27-08:00","id":1036140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1035840#post1035840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I opted out of going to my local march because I didn't hvae a group to go with and got freaked out at the prospect of violence. Feeling pretty damn guilty, but really proud of all the women who did attend.</div> </div> </div> </div> I've heard no reports of violence at these marches, if you wish to attend I believe you will be perfectly safe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T10:11:52-08:00","id":1036141,"title":"","content":"Honestly I don't believe these marches will achieve anything, BUT if these crowds can be harnessed during the midterm elections, Trumps influenced maybe curtailed in 2 years time and then he maybe stopped from getting a second term.<br /> <br /> Hopefully they keep their focus on Trump and genuine women's issues like access to abortion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T10:45:38-08:00","id":1036158,"title":"","content":"So I noticed yesterday and today that when I flipped on the news channels or looked on the news websites, they spent most of their time talking about, and their top articles focused more on, Trump's inauguration numbers and the argument between the White House and news stations over it. The Women's March was basically an afterthought - &quot;Oh, there were millions of women who came out for a march today, but the <i>real</i> story is how Trump had a smaller crowd at his inauguration than Obama, won't admit it, and we caught him lying about it!&quot;<br /> <br /> Which is <b>really fucking frustrating.</b> You'd think by now the media would realize that trying to play &quot;gotcha&quot; with Trump isn't going to do any good - they've spent the last two years trying to do that. They should have spent their time focusing on the Women's March, not wasting time on a dick waving contest with Trump over who had bigger crowds at presidential inaugurations (because seriously, <i>that's</i> the real news?) while pretty much sidelining coverage of the Women's March in comparison.<br /> <br /> The Women's March should have been one of the biggest stories of the year considering how many women across the world joined in solidarity, and I found that it was seriously overshadowed by some pointless bullshit. Christ, I've gotten so sick and tired of seeing Trump say or tweet some stupid piece of bullshit and then watching as the media rushes after that without bothering to focus on anything else, to the detriment of the much, much more important news that occurred during that news cycle.<br /> <br /> I'll give MSNBC credit, they spent a good amount of time focused on the Women's March. But CNN, Fox, and pretty much all the rest of the major news channels spent far more time discussing Trump's inauguration crowds than they did on the Women's March. And that's bullshit.<br /> <br /> *EDIT* I mean, for fuck's sake, if you're going to talk about Trump's inauguration numbers, then at least spend the time talking about how, when the US Park Service tweeted out a unflattering photo comparing Obama and Trump's inaugurations, the Trump administration responded by ordering the US Park Service to effectively <i>close down its Twitter account.</i><br /> <br /> Basically, &quot;If you're not going to say something nice about me, I won't let you say anything at all,&quot; which is something that every American should see as pretty fucking scary. But even <i>that</i> barely got a mention on any of the news stations I watched, and on most internet news sites it was buried under other articles talking about how what the WH press secretary said or on little graphs comparing Washington D.C. subway ride numbers between 2009, 2013 and 2017.<br /> <br /> I really just don't fucking know anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 01-22-2017, 02:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T12:07:13-08:00","id":1036212,"title":"","content":"The unfortunate truth is that news networks are businesses, and they make their money by selling advertising. If the latest dumbass thing Donald has done consistently gets more views than news that actually matters, they'll report the latest dumbass thing Donald has done. Every time. There's really no good solution to this, except to turn the news off when it reports on frivolous bullshit and hope enough people do the same to make frivolous bullshit less profitable than real news. Support news sources that operate on subscription models instead of advertising models, since they don't have to rely as much on pandering for views.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T13:59:28-08:00","id":1036265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1036158#post1036158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I noticed yesterday and today that when I flipped on the news channels or looked on the news websites, they spent most of their time talking about, and their top articles focused more on, Trump's inauguration numbers and the argument between the White House and news stations over it. The Women's March was basically an afterthought - &amp;quot;Oh, there were millions of women who came out for a march today, but the <i>real</i> story is how Trump had a smaller crowd at his inauguration than Obama, won't admit it, and we caught him lying about it!&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Which is <b>really fucking frustrating.</b> You'd think by now the media would realize that trying to play &amp;quot;gotcha&amp;quot; with Trump isn't going to do any good - they've spent the last two years trying to do that. They should have spent their time focusing on the Women's March, not wasting time on a dick waving contest with Trump over who had bigger crowds at presidential inaugurations (because seriously, <i>that's</i> the real news?) while pretty much sidelining coverage of the Women's March in comparison.<br /> <br /> The Women's March should have been one of the biggest stories of the year considering how many women across the world joined in solidarity, and I found that it was seriously overshadowed by some pointless bullshit. Christ, I've gotten so sick and tired of seeing Trump say or tweet some stupid piece of bullshit and then watching as the media rushes after that without bothering to focus on anything else, to the detriment of the much, much more important news that occurred during that news cycle.<br /> <br /> I'll give MSNBC credit, they spent a good amount of time focused on the Women's March. But CNN, Fox, and pretty much all the rest of the major news channels spent far more time discussing Trump's inauguration crowds than they did on the Women's March. And that's bullshit.<br /> <br /> *EDIT* I mean, for fuck's sake, if you're going to talk about Trump's inauguration numbers, then at least spend the time talking about how, when the US Park Service tweeted out a unflattering photo comparing Obama and Trump's inaugurations, the Trump administration responded by ordering the US Park Service to effectively <i>close down its Twitter account.</i><br /> <br /> Basically, &amp;quot;If you're not going to say something nice about me, I won't let you say anything at all,&amp;quot; which is something that every American should see as pretty fucking scary. But even <i>that</i> barely got a mention on any of the news stations I watched, and on most internet news sites it was buried under other articles talking about how what the WH press secretary said or on little graphs comparing Washington D.C. subway ride numbers between 2009, 2013 and 2017.<br /> <br /> I really just don't fucking know anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'll point out that some of those journalists are women so are they waving dicks too? <br /> <br /> Look it's a lot of women, but how much more is there to say then they're a lot of women out there and these are the major concerns that have? <br /> <br /> These women and there numbers will matter more during election times. <br /> <br /> Just a thought that occurred to me, but might Trump have deliberately picked a fight with the media to distract from the women's March or am I giving him too much credit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T16:10:57-08:00","id":1036322,"title":"","content":"Your media at least noticed that this march exists. While not feminist-related, Poland has a tradition of Great Orchestra Of Christmas Charity ( <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Great_Orchestra_of_Christmas_Charity\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Great_...istmas_Charity</a> ) . Our current ruling party doesn't like them because Catholic Church dislikes them - and Catholic Church dislikes them because the main guy of Christmas Charity also does Woodstock Festival in Summer, which of course is seen as a unholy spawn of devil. Ruling party was endorsed by Church which was a major part of their victory, so they are now paying off their &quot;political debt&quot;to the Church. <br /> So, this year, our national/public TV tried to erase the Christmas Charity from the public perception by ignoring it's existence and not mentioning it at all, and even better, actively removing Christmas Charity's symbols and logos from any footage that had them in. It wasn't a small event - for Poland, this was (yet again) a record breaking charity event unlike anything else that happens here. So...yeah. At least no one tried to deny that march existed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T17:49:04-08:00","id":1036364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1036212#post1036212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The unfortunate truth is that news networks are businesses, and they make their money by selling advertising. If the latest dumbass thing Donald has done consistently gets more views than news that actually matters, they'll report the latest dumbass thing Donald has done. Every time. There's really no good solution to this, except to turn the news off when it reports on frivolous bullshit and hope enough people do the same to make frivolous bullshit less profitable than real news. Support news sources that operate on subscription models instead of advertising models, since they don't have to rely as much on pandering for views.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, there is a solution - lobby the news networks directly. If they receive a multitude of letters, emails, or even active protestors asking the question, &quot;WHY DON'T YOU REPORT ON [subject]!?&quot; that will show them that there is a demand.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1036265#post1036265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a thought that occurred to me, but might Trump have deliberately picked a fight with the media to distract from the women's March or am I giving him too much credit?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd err on the side of &quot;too much credit.&quot; Ol' Donny Boy picks fights with the media pretty much constantly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T18:13:12-08:00","id":1036380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\">