:{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T05:17:40-08:00","id":1036550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1036417#post1036417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Anyways where do these women go from here, what's the next step.</div> </div> </div> </div>Keep up the energy and momentum until midterm elections. Our local PSR group set up committees for various issues. Once I untangle myself from other responsibilities, I'm going to join either the Local Elections committee or the Gerrymandering committee. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T10:20:13-08:00","id":1036696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://i.imgtc.com/vMYOqhf.png\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://i.imgtc.com/vMYOqhf.png\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://i.imgtc.com/vMYOqhf.png\" target=\"_blank\"> https://i.imgtc.com/vMYOqhf.png </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> One of the applauded speakers of the women's March went to prison for years for raping, torturing, and murdering a gay man, WTF. <br /> <br /> Please tell me I'm missing something and it's not true, because holy fuck, that is a huge betrayal of the GLBT community.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T11:06:10-08:00","id":1036720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1036265#post1036265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a thought that occurred to me, but might Trump have deliberately picked a fight with the media to distract from the women's March or am I giving him too much credit?</div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn't be a surprise. Trump's done the same thing numerous times before, saying something stupid or controversial in order to get the media talking about it instead of something worse. Even if it wasn't intentional, <a href=\"http://money.cnn.com/2017/01/22/media/alternative-facts-donald-trump/index.html\" target=\"_blank\">his administration clearly understands how he benefited from it.</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The administration is likely not all that upset with the discussion it's started among the press about the truth and its flaunting of it. The Trump aide, speaking on condition of anonymity, pointed out a fringe benefit of the administration's media complaints: &quot;By going out and doing this, it took images of people protesting off the TV.&quot; </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T11:06:10-08:00","id":1036721,"title":"","content":"Double posted for some reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T11:21:05-08:00","id":1036727,"title":"","content":"It's a little disheartening to be reminded of how trans-exclusionary a lot of mainstream feminism still is. These marches are still 100% a good thing, but it's real tough to see how vagina-centric a lot of the protesting was and how some marches apparently had TERFs out in force.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T11:33:29-08:00","id":1036741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1036727#post1036727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a little disheartening to be reminded of how trans-exclusionary a lot of mainstream feminism still is. These marches are still 100% a good thing, but it's real tough to see how vagina-centric a lot of the protesting was and how some marches apparently had TERFs out in force.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A major part of the protests relate to Women's health (birth control, abortions, pap shears, and the like). Thus, I'm not really surprised that uteri were plastered all over everyone's protest posters.<br /> <br /> I'm ashamed to say I didn't consider how those types of posters would affect trans-people. I was looking at it from the point of view of &quot;bringing female sex organs out hushed conversations&quot;. I think removing the mysticism of female sexual organs would allow them to get the medical care they deserve.<br /> <br /> What does TERF stand for?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 01-23-2017, 02:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T12:12:40-08:00","id":1036759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1036741#post1036741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> A major part of the protests relate to Women's health (birth control, abortions, pap shears, and the like). Thus, I'm not really surprised that uteri were plastered all over everyone's protest posters.<br /> <br /> I'm ashamed to say I didn't consider how those types of posters would affect trans-people. I was looking at it from the point of view of &amp;quot;bringing female sex organs out hushed conversations&amp;quot;. I think removing the mysticism of female sexual organs would allow them to get the medical care they deserve.<br /> <br /> What does TERF stand for?</div> </div> </div> </div>I know that a large part of these protests is based around attacks on Planned Parenthood/contraception/abortion and as a backlash to Trump's pussy-grabbing nonsense, but that still serves as an unpleasant reminder that most of the world still doesn't see women with penises as women.<br /> <br /> Trans-Exclusionary Radical Feminist, feminists who think transgender women are just men trying to invade female spaces and that transgender men are just confused women. Any time you see some asshat trot out the line &quot;biological woman,&quot; you're dealing with a TERF.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T12:13:38-08:00","id":1036760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1036741#post1036741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> A major part of the protests relate to Women's health (birth control, abortions, pap shears, and the like). Thus, I'm not really surprised that uteri were plastered all over everyone's protest posters.<br /> <br /> I'm ashamed to say I didn't consider how those types of posters would affect trans-people. I was looking at it from the point of view of &quot;bringing female sex organs out hushed conversations&quot;. I think removing the mysticism of female sexual organs would allow them to get the medical care they deserve.<br /> <br /> What does TERF stand for?</div> </div> </div> </div>Trans-Exclusionary Radical Feminist. They're those bad feminists you keep hearing about who think women are nothing more than walking wombs, men are nothing more than pillaging rapists, with transwomen their spies and transmen as their hapless sycophants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T15:01:30-08:00","id":1036857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1036760#post1036760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Trans-Exclusionary Radical Feminist. They're those bad feminists you keep hearing about who think women are nothing more than walking wombs, men are nothing more than pillaging rapists, with transwomen their spies and transmen as their hapless sycophants.</div> </div> </div> </div>You may also hear &quot;TWERF&quot; to refer to some who accept trans men... as women... but still hate trans women as men.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T23:39:41-08:00","id":1037061,"title":"","content":"The language, &quot;female sex organs&quot; is also trans-unfriendly, implying (usually unintentionally) that the sex organs of trans women are not &quot;female,&quot; and that the sex organs of trans men are &quot;female.&quot; Especially if the goal is to demystify said organs and destroy the taboo around discussing them openly, we should just call them vaginas/uteri/labia/ovaries/etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T05:43:32-08:00","id":1037135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1037061#post1037061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The language, &quot;female sex organs&quot; is also trans-unfriendly, implying (usually unintentionally) that the sex organs of trans women are not &quot;female,&quot; and that the sex organs of trans men are &quot;female.&quot; Especially if the goal is to demystify said organs and destroy the taboo around discussing them openly, we should just call them vaginas/uteri/labia/ovaries/etc.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sorry, I didn't mean to offend. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Probably my Catholic upbringing rearing its ugly head.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T06:05:05-08:00","id":1037147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1037061#post1037061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The language, &quot;female sex organs&quot; is also trans-unfriendly, implying (usually unintentionally) that the sex organs of trans women are not &quot;female,&quot; and that the sex organs of trans men are &quot;female.&quot; Especially if the goal is to demystify said organs and destroy the taboo around discussing them openly, we should just call them vaginas/uteri/labia/ovaries/etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find this perspective confusing. Is the intention here to entirely divorce gender from biological characteristics?<br /> <br /> If so, what does it even mean to have a &quot;gender&quot;? What distinguishes &quot;gender&quot; from any other kind of cultural role?*<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">To clarify where I'm coming from:<br /> I believe sex and gender are inextricably tied together, and that is <i>as it should be</i>, if for no other reason than for linguistic convenience. Individuals can identify as whatever gender they choose, and there is no moral implication in that choice. There is, however, a tacit assumption that in choosing a gender they are aligning themselves with a cultural role associated with a given sex. In a sense, having a cisgender identitity is the assumed &quot;default.&quot;<br /> <br /> There are innumerable roles a person can take on or have assigned to them that have no connection to sex. I use the word &quot;gender&quot; <i>solely</i> to refer to those roles tied to sex.<br /> <br /> Like wonderandawe, I was raised Catholic, but I think my perspective comes more from wanting clear categories to describe people rather than from anything else. In the absense of a widely-accepted language for describing the breadth of the gender spectrum, I'm determined to continue using &quot;gender&quot; as a sex-oriented term.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":908,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","user":"semicasual","date":". 01-24-2017, 09:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T06:39:21-08:00","id":1037158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1037147#post1037147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find this perspective confusing. Is the intention here to entirely divorce gender from biological characteristics?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, because gender is literally a social construct.<br /> <br /> The things you put in your spoiler are articles of faith, and are not remotely based on science. I urge you to go buy the gender issue of National Geographic immediately. Here's a preview of what you'll see:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.nationalgeographic.com/magazine/2017/01/how-science-helps-us-understand-gender-identity/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://i.natgeofe.com/n/96ac2eb6-40dd-46dd-9643-762af0729887/genderidentity_09_16x9.jpg?w=1200\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.nationalgeographic.com/magazine/2017/01/how-science-helps-us-understand-gender-identity/\" target=\"_blank\"> How science is helping us understand gender </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.nationalgeographic.com/magazine/2017/01/how-science-helps-us-understand-gender-identity/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.nationalgeographic.com/magazine/2017/01/how-science-helps-us-understand-gender-identity/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Freed from the binary of boy and girl, gender identity is a shifting landscape. Can science help us navigate? </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T07:05:16-08:00","id":1037179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1037158#post1037158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, because gender is literally a social construct.<br /> <br /> The things you put in your spoiler are articles of faith, and are not remotely based on science. I urge you to go buy the gender issue of National Geographic immediately. Here's a preview of what you'll see:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.nationalgeographic.com/magazine/2017/01/how-science-helps-us-understand-gender-identity/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.nationalgeographic.com/ma...nder-identity/</a></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think I mentioned faith or science, and I did acknowledge that gender is a cultural thing rather than a biological thing.<br /> <br /> Let me try some different questions. Why does gender <i>need </i> to be divorced from biology? Would that not effectively make the word &quot;gender&quot; meaningless? Is it inherently wrong to have a cultural role or expectations attached to biological characteristics, if they are nonbinding?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":908,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","user":"semicasual","date":". 01-24-2017, 10:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T07:53:05-08:00","id":1037203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1036727#post1036727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a little disheartening to be reminded of how trans-exclusionary a lot of mainstream feminism still is. These marches are still 100% a good thing, but it's real tough to see how vagina-centric a lot of the protesting was and how some marches apparently had TERFs out in force.</div> </div> </div> </div> Welcome to feminism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T08:09:24-08:00","id":1037215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1037203#post1037203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Welcome to feminism.</div> </div> </div> </div>You of all people don't get to take that tone, <i>MRA</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T08:18:30-08:00","id":1037229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1037158#post1037158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, because gender is literally a social construct.<br /> <br /> The things you put in your spoiler are articles of faith, and are not remotely based on science. I urge you to go buy the gender issue of National Geographic immediately. Here's a preview of what you'll see:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.nationalgeographic.com/magazine/2017/01/how-science-helps-us-understand-gender-identity/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.nationalgeographic.com/ma...nder-identity/</a></div> </div> </div> </div> Bullshit, if Gender was completely a cultural thing then the Transgendered wouldn't exist, they've done brain scans of people who are Transgender and showed that there brains resemble the Gender they see them selves as.<br /> <br /> People confuse Gender and cultural based Gender expressions, they are not the same thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T08:52:03-08:00","id":1037241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1037229#post1037229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Bullshit, if Gender was completely a cultural thing then the Transgendered wouldn't exist, they've done brain scans of people who are Transgender and showed that there brains resemble the Gender they see them selves as.<br /> <br /> People confuse Gender and cultural based Gender expressions, they are not the same thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reread the article I linked to. There is a brain pattern that is common among men. <i>Some</i> transmen have that brain pattern, some don't. There is a brain pattern that is common among women. <i>Some</i> transwomen have that pattern, some don't. It's not entirely clear that that brain pattern is sex-linked at all. The problem we have is that we have this mental model:<br /> <br /> XX -&gt; female, uterus, breasts, woman, mommy, skirt, makeup, pink<br /> XY -&gt; male, penis, beard, man, daddy, suit, crew cut, blue<br /> <br /> But in reality, everyone's DNA is pushing them toward male <i>and</i> female. The Y chromosome's presence <i>usually</i> puts its finger so hard on the male scale that you get beard, penis and its absence <i>usually</i> puts its finger so hard on the female scale that you get breasts, uterus. But nothing that comes from your DNA gets you to &quot;woman, mommy, skirt, makeup, pink&quot; or &quot;man, daddy, suit, crew cut, blue&quot;. <i>That</i> is gender. And you need look no further than the numerous cultures mentioned in the article I linked to that have multiple genders to see that even just &quot;man&quot; and &quot;woman&quot; are purely cultural constructs.<br /> <br /> But wait, you say, if that's all that gender is, then why do people have sex reassignment surgery? Why bother with bottom or even top surgery if all you have to do is change the letter on your driver's license from M to F or vice versa? Why should we consider it more important than cosmetic surgery? Because the scale isn't either/or. There's multiple facets, internal and external, of our biologies and psyches, and a significant mismatch between them can cause harm <i>all by itself</i>. And surgery is one method to correct that mismatch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":707,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","user":"etherial","date":". 01-24-2017, 11:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T08:59:39-08:00","id":1037244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1037215#post1037215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You of all people don't get to take that tone, <i>MRA</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div> I post a link that showed that one of the key Speakers who got applauded at the Women's March was convicted of raping, torturing, and murdering a gay man, and she was complaining how terribly unfair to women it is that she went to prison for raping torturing, and murdering someone and she got applauses, she's being treated like a fucking hero.<br /> <br /> You have much bigger issues then my tone that you should be worried about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T09:16:28-08:00","id":1037250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1037244#post1037244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I post a link that showed that one of the key Speakers who got applauded at the Women's March was convicted of raping, torturing, and murdering a gay man, and she was complaining how terribly unfair to women it is that she went to prison for raping torturing, and murdering someone and she got applauses, she's being treated like a fucking hero.<br /> <br /> You have much bigger issues then my tone that you should be worried about.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right, we do. But those problems aren't fundamental to feminism. As opposed to the hate group you so proudly claim membership in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T10:05:49-08:00","id":1037268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1037135#post1037135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, I didn't mean to offend. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Probably my Catholic upbringing rearing its ugly head.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, no offense was taken <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Most folks who aren't deeply stepped in trans issues don't even think about it, and it's not their fault for not knowing the language we've all been raised hearing and using is inherently trans-unfriendly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1037147#post1037147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find this perspective confusing. Is the intention here to entirely divorce gender from biological characteristics?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. As etherial pointed out, gender is a cultural construct, so it shouldn't be so bound up in biology.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1037147#post1037147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If so, what does it even mean to have a &amp;quot;gender&amp;quot;? What distinguishes &amp;quot;gender&amp;quot; from any other kind of cultural role?*</div> </div> </div> </div>Gender <i>is</i> a cultural role. Why does it need to be distinguished from other cultural roles, other than &quot;that's the way it's always been?&quot; And if that's the only reason, why is it more important to adhere to that tradition than to allow people who's identities align with a particular role to take it on without being stigmatized because of their biology? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1037147#post1037147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To clarify where I'm coming from:<br /> I believe sex and gender are inextricably tied together, and that is <i>as it should be</i>, if for no other reason than for linguistic convenience. Individuals can identify as whatever gender they choose, and there is no moral implication in that choice. There is, however, a tacit assumption that in choosing a gender they are aligning themselves with a cultural role associated with a given sex. In a sense, having a cisgender identitity is the assumed &amp;quot;default.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Why is linguistic convenience more important to you than the legitimacy of trans people's identities? Why does there need to be an &quot;assumed default&quot; when it comes to gender?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1037147#post1037147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are innumerable roles a person can take on or have assigned to them that have no connection to sex. I use the word &amp;quot;gender&amp;quot; <i>solely</i> to refer to those roles tied to sex.</div> </div> </div> </div>But there is nothing about gender roles that is inherently tied to sex, beyond it being the cultural norm. If that cultural norm is harmful to people who's identities don't align with the ones they were assigned on the basis of their sex, then it's a bad cultural norm to have.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1037147#post1037147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like wonderandawe, I was raised Catholic, but I think my perspective comes more from wanting clear categories to describe people rather than from anything else. In the absense of a widely-accepted language for describing the breadth of the gender spectrum, I'm determined to continue using &amp;quot;gender&amp;quot; as a sex-oriented term.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;It's inconvenient for me to stop using language that is harmful to you&quot; is not a good reason to continue using that language.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T10:11:50-08:00","id":1037270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1037179#post1037179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let me try some different questions. Why does gender <i>need </i> to be divorced from biology?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because its association with biology alienates and harms trans people.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1037179#post1037179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would that not effectively make the word &quot;gender&quot; meaningless?</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, in a perfect world I don't think we would need a concept of gender at all. But, we don't live in a perfect world, roles and expectations on the basis of gender do exist, and people who's identities fall within those cultural roles should have those identities respected and not stigmatized on the unrelated basis of their anatomy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1037179#post1037179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it inherently wrong to have a cultural role or expectations attached to biological characteristics, if they are nonbinding?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T10:35:42-08:00","id":1037284,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>\u200bKnock off the combative exchanges or I will lock the thread and suspend people. </b></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T11:04:00-08:00","id":1037297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1037268#post1037268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;It's inconvenient for me to stop using language that is harmful to you&quot; is not a good reason to continue using that language.</div> </div> </div> </div>What if the only alternative is A) to be unable to communicate or B) to disrespect the self-identity of another, different group of people? To me, that appears to be the choice I'm being presented with.<br /> <br /> For what it is worth, I intend no harm. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1037270#post1037270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, in a perfect world I don't think we would need a concept of gender at all. But, we don't live in a perfect world, roles and expectations on the basis of gender do exist, and people who's identities fall within those cultural roles should have those identities respected and not stigmatized on the unrelated basis of their anatomy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you believe it is possible to entirely disconnect a person's identity from their physical form?<br /> <br /> Followup question: do you believe a person's identity is defined <i>solely</i> by how they choose to describe themselves?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T11:10:22-08:00","id":1037301,"title":"","content":"I'm probably getting this wrong but please bare with me. Is gender and sexuality really completely divorced from biology? I agree for the most part that gender, in regards to masculinity and femininity, are subjective cultural roles and identities that people are indoctrinated into accepting, but I have trouble trying to understand that in relation to trans people. When a transman feels that they're a man that's born with a female body is that response a consequence of their sexuality, which I assume to be a biology function that they're both with, or is it rejection of assigned societal gender roles and identities? Is it both?<br /> <br /> I ask this because it seems that many transpeople not only surgical correct their bodies but also adopt cultural identities of masculinity and femininity.<br /> <br /> I hope this question makes sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1675,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","user":"Weirdboyz","date":". 01-24-2017, 02:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T11:11:57-08:00","id":1037303,"title":"","content":"I've done some thinking.<br /> <br /> I believe the issue is that the Woman's March represented both Female Gender Issues (lower pay, sexual abuse, slut shaming, etc) and Female Sex Issues (Abortion, Access to Birth Control, etc). For most of the March's participants, they are both of female gender and sex. For them, there is no separation between sex and gender, thus feel no need to acknowledge this separation. <br /> <br /> Feel free to correct me if I am off base.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T11:13:43-08:00","id":1037305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1037241#post1037241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reread the article I linked to. There is a brain pattern that is common among men. <i>Some</i> transmen have that brain pattern, some don't. There is a brain pattern that is common among women. <i>Some</i> transwomen have that pattern, some don't. It's not entirely clear that that brain pattern is sex-linked at all. The problem we have is that we have this mental model:<br /> <br /> XX -&gt; female, uterus, breasts, woman, mommy, skirt, makeup, pink<br /> XY -&gt; male, penis, beard, man, daddy, suit, crew cut, blue<br /> <br /> But in reality, everyone's DNA is pushing them toward male <i>and</i> female. The Y chromosome's presence <i>usually</i> puts its finger so hard on the male scale that you get beard, penis and its absence <i>usually</i> puts its finger so hard on the female scale that you get breasts, uterus. But nothing that comes from your DNA gets you to &quot;woman, mommy, skirt, makeup, pink&quot; or &quot;man, daddy, suit, crew cut, blue&quot;. <i>That</i> is gender. And you need look no further than the numerous cultures mentioned in the article I linked to that have multiple genders to see that even just &quot;man&quot; and &quot;woman&quot; are purely cultural constructs.<br /> <br /> But wait, you say, if that's all that gender is, then why do people have sex reassignment surgery? Why bother with bottom or even top surgery if all you have to do is change the letter on your driver's license from M to F or vice versa? Why should we consider it more important than cosmetic surgery? Because the scale isn't either/or. There's multiple facets, internal and external, of our biologies and psyches, and a significant mismatch between them can cause harm <i>all by itself</i>. And surgery is one method to correct that mismatch.</div> </div> </div> </div> I agree that things are complex, but that doesn't mean there isn't a biological compenent to gender, it's very complex, and unique to the individual.<br /> <br /> Acknowledging there is a biological element to gender doesn't need to harm the transgender community as long as one acknowledges that genders have plenty of variations.<br /> <br /> Science has to be our guide and we need far more unbiased research on this topic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 01-24-2017, 02:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T11:22:47-08:00","id":1037310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1037061#post1037061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The language, &quot;female sex organs&quot; is also trans-unfriendly, implying (usually unintentionally) that the sex organs of trans women are not &quot;female,&quot; and that the sex organs of trans men are &quot;female.&quot; Especially if the goal is to demystify said organs and destroy the taboo around discussing them openly, we should just call them vaginas/uteri/labia/ovaries/etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Out of curiosity, if both &quot;female&quot; and &quot;woman/women&quot; (and likewise male and man/men) all describe gender rather than biological sex, what would be the appropriate words for describing the individuals born with certain biological sexual characteristics?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T11:46:13-08:00","id":1037330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1037297#post1037297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if the only alternative is A) to be unable to communicate or B) to disrespect the self-identity of another, different group of people? To me, that appears to be the choice I'm being presented with.</div> </div> </div> </div>We are constantly having to face choices like this, unfortunately. The correct answer does depend on context. Sometimes it is appropriate to refrain from communicating on a particular subject in a particular context. For instance, on these forums, group attacks are against the rules, so I generally try to avoid discussing groups about which I have a difficult time saying anything but negative things. However, when it is appropriate and/or important to communicate about a particular issue but that communication isn't possible without harming someone, you have to assess who what you have to say will harm, how it will harm them, and who is most able to bear the harm that will be done to them. For instance, if the choice is between offending someone, or contributing to an ongoing systematic injustice against an oppressed group, the former is the lesser evil.<br /> <br /> Out of curiosity, who's identity is harmed by using the word &quot;vagina&quot; instead of the term &quot;female sex organ&quot;?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1037297#post1037297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For what it is worth, I intend no harm.</div> </div> </div> </div>I assumed as much. And the lack of intent to harm is certainly appreciated. Unfortunately, it's a side-effect of language that the things we say often cause harm in spite of our intent. The key is to strive to minimize the harm we cause, rather than to use lack of intent as an excuse for the harm we cause.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1037297#post1037297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you believe it is possible to entirely disconnect a person's identity from their physical form?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, certainly not. Our identities are constantly being shaped by all manner of influences, including our physical forms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1037297#post1037297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Followup question: do you believe a person's identity is defined <i>solely</i> by how they choose to describe themselves?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, but I do believe that we are all the ultimate authorities on our own identities. No one can know how you feel better than you do, so whether or not saying you are X makes you X, it would be wrong of someone else to say, &quot;no, you're Y.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T11:48:30-08:00","id":1037332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1037310#post1037310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Out of curiosity, if both &quot;female&quot; and &quot;woman/women&quot; (and likewise male and man/men) all describe gender rather than biological sex, what would be the appropriate words for describing the individuals born with certain biological sexual characteristics?</div> </div> </div> </div>Assigned male/female at birth.<br /> <br /> EDIT: The abbreviations AMAB (pronounced a-mab) and AFAB (pronounced a-fab) also work, since assigned male/female at birth is a bit of a mouthful to use in casual conversations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 01-24-2017, 02:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T11:52:38-08:00","id":1037333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1037303#post1037303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've done some thinking.<br /> <br /> I believe the issue is that the Woman's March represented both Female Gender Issues (lower pay, sexual abuse, slut shaming, etc) and Female Sex Issues (Abortion, Access to Birth Control, etc). For most of the March's participants, they are both of female gender and sex. For them, there is no separation between sex and gender, thus feel no need to acknowledge this separation. <br /> <br /> Feel free to correct me if I am off base.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's totally spot-on.<br /> <br /> I do think there was also a fair share of intentional trans exclusionism going on as well, but I agree that this is really the root of the issue for the significant majority. That's why I believe it's so important to spread trans awareness and to have discussions like this about why associating womanhood with uteri is harmful to trans women and what can be done to improve on the language we use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T11:57:46-08:00","id":1037335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://toysoldier.wordpress.com/2017/01/24/feminists-still-cant-take-a-joke/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://s0.wp.com/i/blank.jpg?m=1383295312i\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://toysoldier.wordpress.com/2017/01/24/feminists-still-cant-take-a-joke/\" target=\"_blank\"> Feminists still can&rsquo;t take a joke </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://toysoldier.wordpress.com/2017/01/24/feminists-still-cant-take-a-joke/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://toysoldier.wordpress.com/2017/01/24/feminists-still-cant-take-a-joke/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Piers Morgan gave brilliant response to the women&rsquo;s marches held on Saturday: The amount of whining and complaining about the joke tweet was incredible. Hundreds of people tripped over themse&hellip; </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T12:02:59-08:00","id":1037339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1037335#post1037335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://toysoldier.wordpress.com/2017/01/24/feminists-still-cant-take-a-joke/\" target=\"_blank\">https://toysoldier.wordpress.com/201...t-take-a-joke/</a></div> </div> </div> </div>It helps when jokes are actually funny. That tweet was not.<br /> <br /> Also, haven't you been warned to stop posting links with no context and no other content?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T12:29:31-08:00","id":1037359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1037333#post1037333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that's totally spot-on.<br /> <br /> I do think there was also a fair share of intentional trans exclusionism going on as well, but I agree that this is really the root of the issue for the significant majority. That's why I believe it's so important to spread trans awareness and to have discussions like this about why associating womanhood with uteri is harmful to trans women and what can be done to improve on the language we use.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In what ways could the Woman's March be more friendly to Transwoman? <br /> <br /> While the movement could be more welcoming to Transwoman, I personally believe AFAB issues should be protested at a Woman's March. I agree that not all woman have uteri. Besides Transwoman, some AFAB woman no longer have a Uterus. But the Majority do have a Uterus and if you remove Reproductive Health from Woman's Rights movement, you may lose supporters. Segmenting the issues between Woman Sex and Woman gender issues would do more harm than good. <br /> <br /> I don't know. This could be my desperation talking. To be honest, the point of the Uterus signs is to make people uncomfortable. You weren't the intended target of this, but rather the idiots on Capitol Hill who want to regulate Reproductive Health for religious reasons. I was so focused on those fuckers, I didn't even consider how Transwomen would feel. I apologize for this. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T12:31:05-08:00","id":1037360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1037330#post1037330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Out of curiosity, who's identity is harmed by using the word &quot;vagina&quot; instead of the term &quot;female sex organ&quot;?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I would think &quot;nobody.&quot; But then again, I would also think that &quot;sex is female, gender identity is male, expression is male&quot; (AKA S:F/G:M/E:M) is a harmless-yet-comprehensive way to describe someone. Apparently not for everyone?...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1037330#post1037330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, certainly not. Our identities are constantly being shaped by all manner of influences, including our physical forms.<br /> ...<br /> No, but I do believe that we are all the ultimate authorities on our own identities. No one can know how you feel better than you do, so whether or not saying you are X makes you X, it would be wrong of someone else to say, &quot;no, you're Y.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree, for two reasons. <br /> 1. Just because I am the ultimate authority on myself doesn't mean my capacity for self-awareness is any good.<br /> 2. As a participant in a society of people, and as a creature whose creation was not of my own will, neither my form nor my function is decided wholly by me.<br /> <br /> To some extent, my being is defined by external forces. I feel it is only reasonable to accept that who and what I am is not for me to determine alone. If someone or something tells me &quot;You're Y!&quot; when I think I'm X, then I might be in the position of needing to &quot;prove&quot; that I am X. Or maybe they need to prove that I'm Y. Context changes how that exchange goes, but in any case I can't take my self-identity for granted or insist that other people accept it without question. I need to be prepared to either assert my identity against resistance, or accept a different definition for myself. <br /> <br /> As far as this applies to language, my thinking is that transpeople need to do one of two things:<br /> 1. Change the definitions of existing words until they fit easily within those definitions. <br /> 2. Find different words to define themselves, and assert those words until they become commonly accepted. <br /> <br /> ...I suspect that this is all a bit more abstract than what you were originally aiming for, which was &quot;Transmen/women should be acknowledged as real men/women.&quot; If so, I apologize for the tangent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T12:48:39-08:00","id":1037371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1037332#post1037332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Assigned male/female at birth.<br /> <br /> EDIT: The abbreviations AMAB (pronounced a-mab) and AFAB (pronounced a-fab) also work, since assigned male/female at birth is a bit of a mouthful to use in casual conversations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, thanks for the heads up.<br /> <br /> A couple of years ago I was in a conversation with two of my trans friends, and they told me that male and female refer to biology (whether you have a penis or a vagina), whereas man and woman refer to gender, which creates a grid - you could have a male woman (that is, a woman with a penis) or a female man (a man with a vagina), or a female woman (a woman with a vagina) or a male man (a man with a penis).<br /> <br /> This was also why it was okay to refer use male and female as a way to refer to other species (we used fish since I was working in a fish market at the time and sometimes it was important to differentiate them based on their biological sexual organs, so we had male and female fish) but you obviously wouldn't refer to fish as &quot;men&quot; or &quot;women&quot; since fish don't really have the sort of concept of gender social-roles in the same way that humans do.<br /> <br /> So I've spent the last couple of years operating under the impression that that's how it was supposed to work.<br /> <br /> Then I guess my follow up question is, when discussing animals (I'll use my fish again) if male and female refer to gender rather than biological sex, those words wouldn't apply (fish obviously don't have the social construct known as gender), so I guess you would use Assigned Male/Female at Birth to refer to the two sexes of fish as well? So a fish with a vagina full of eggs would be an AFAB fish and a fish with a penis would be an AMAB fish?<br /> <br /> Not trying be a jerk or anything, just trying to wrap my head around how all this is supposed to work out after several years of apparently not understanding it nearly as well as I thought I did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T13:05:23-08:00","id":1037386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1037359#post1037359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In what ways could the Woman's March be more friendly to Transwoman? <br /> <br /> While the movement could be more welcoming to Transwoman, I personally believe AFAB issues should be protested at a Woman's March. I agree that not all woman have uteri. Besides Transwoman, some AFAB woman no longer have a Uterus. But the Majority do have a Uterus and if you remove Reproductive Health from Woman's Rights movement, you may lose supporters. Segmenting the issues between Woman Sex and Woman gender issues would do more harm than good.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. It's a complicated issue and I don't know what the solution is. I do think the women's march was good for what it was. I think a lot of trans women just need to be able to vent their frustration about feeling alienated in a movement that was at least in part about female solidarity. And I think we should utilize this opportunity to talk more about what role sex plays in gender. Like, you've started saying AFAB issues instead of female reproductive issues, which is in my opinion a positive thing to have come out of the march. We're still at a stage in trans issues where what's needed is to spread awareness and information. And this is helping us do that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1037359#post1037359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know. This could be my desperation talking. To be honest, the point of the Uterus signs is to make people uncomfortable. You weren't the intended target of this, but rather the idiots on Capitol Hill who want to regulate Reproductive Health for religious reasons. I was so focused on those fuckers, I didn't even consider how Transwomen would feel. I apologize for this.</div> </div> </div> </div>I appreciate it. And like I said, I don't blame you, or anyone at the march who used the opportunity to address AFAB issues, except those (whom I believe were in the minority) who actively want to exclude trans women. That you are willing to listen and discuss it with an open mind, and to apologize for any unintentional harm is more than many people do, and means a lot to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T13:56:56-08:00","id":1037407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1037371#post1037371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, thanks for the heads up.</div> </div> </div> </div>No problem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1037371#post1037371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A couple of years ago I was in a conversation with two of my trans friends, and they told me that male and female refer to biology (whether you have a penis or a vagina), whereas man and woman refer to gender, which creates a grid - you could have a male woman (that is, a woman with a penis) or a female man (a man with a vagina), or a female woman (a woman with a vagina) or a male man (a man with a penis).<br /> <br /> This was also why it was okay to refer use male and female as a way to refer to other species (we used fish since I was working in a fish market at the time and sometimes it was important to differentiate them based on their biological sexual organs, so we had male and female fish) but you obviously wouldn't refer to fish as &quot;men&quot; or &quot;women&quot; since fish don't really have the sort of concept of gender social-roles in the same way that humans do.<br /> <br /> So I've spent the last couple of years operating under the impression that that's how it was supposed to work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, there's unfortunately not really a consensus yet on the best way to discuss gender and transness. Some people, including some trans people do use the &quot;male/female is sex, man/woman is gender&quot; model. I, and a lot of people in the social circles I am involved in, dislike that model for a few reasons. The biggest is that male/female and man/woman are used pretty much interchangeably outside of discussions of trans issues. Also, being described as a male woman would just make me super uncomfortable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1037371#post1037371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then I guess my follow up question is, when discussing animals (I'll use my fish again) if male and female refer to gender rather than biological sex, those words wouldn't apply (fish obviously don't have the social construct known as gender), so I guess you would use Assigned Male/Female at Birth to refer to the two sexes of fish as well? So a fish with a vagina full of eggs would be an AFAB fish and a fish with a penis would be an AMAB fish?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, I just use male and female when discussing animals. AMAB and AFAB don't really make a lot of sense in reference to non-human animals because they don't have a concept of gender (as far as we know) and don't assign genders to their children at birth on the basis of their genitals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1037371#post1037371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not trying be a jerk or anything, just trying to wrap my head around how all this is supposed to work out after several years of apparently not understanding it nearly as well as I thought I did.</div> </div> </div> </div>No worries, they're perfectly reasonable questions to ask and I'm happy to answer as best I can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T14:10:39-08:00","id":1037413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1037407#post1037407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, there's unfortunately not really a consensus yet on the best way to discuss gender and transness. Some people, including some trans people do use the &quot;male/female is sex, man/woman is gender&quot; model. I, and a lot of people in the social circles I am involved in, dislike that model for a few reasons. The biggest is that male/female and man/woman are used pretty much interchangeably outside of discussions of trans issues. Also, being described as a male woman would just make me super uncomfortable.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, this is where I usually get hung up. I honestly feel like I need to learn a new language when discussing trans issues, which comes up rather often in my work (work at a homeless shelter). And that's alright, it's something I know I'm not familiar with in the least and have a lot to learn about before I can comfortably speak on the subject. I suppose the real issue from my perspective is when I get yelled at or harassed for not knowing the proper pronoun to use when talking about or to a specific individual. It's a new topic for me; I need time to learn. And in all fairness, the trans people are (generally speaking, of course) the ones who are understanding and willing to walk me through the new terminology. It's usually the non-trans people trying to be their advocates who lose their ever-loving mind because I said &quot;male&quot; instead of &quot;man&quot; or something along those lines.<br /> <br /> Sorry, mini-rant over.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1037335#post1037335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://toysoldier.wordpress.com/2017/01/24/feminists-still-cant-take-a-joke/\" target=\"_blank\">https://toysoldier.wordpress.com/201...t-take-a-joke/</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Omega, we get it. You don't like feminists. Maybe instead of randomly posting about it in a thread about the women's march and related topics, you can start your own anti-feminist thread, where you can explain the many and varied reasons for your hate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T14:34:23-08:00","id":1037423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1037407#post1037407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nah, I just use male and female when discussing animals. AMAB and AFAB don't really make a lot of sense in reference to non-human animals because they don't have a concept of gender (as far as we know) and don't assign genders to their children at birth on the basis of their genitals.</div> </div> </div> </div>I gotcha.<br /> <br /> I suspect this is going to remain an issue as long as male/female is okay to be used to refer to biology except for when it's not. I imagine that a lot of people, even those who have a fair interest in trans-rights (like myself), or even sometimes trans-individuals themselves, are going to be using language on occasion in ways that make members of the trans community upset. Language is really complicated and so far it doesn't seem as if the trans-community has solid idea yet on what it is acceptable and what isn't (though of course, some things are obviously unacceptable).<br /> <br /> Most likely the women at the march holding up signs talking about, &quot;Female sex organs&quot; weren't specifically excluding trans-women, but were talking about protecting the reproductive rights of people with vaginas and such (and to be fair things like birth control and abortion aren't really something that trans-women have to worry about in quite the same way as someone who was born with a vagina and can get pregnant). Honestly, they probably just weren't aware the female != biology. In a way, it's also a bit similar to how &quot;Black Lives Matter&quot; doesn't mean white lives don't matter - talking about the importance of AFAB sex organs doesn't necessarily mean that trans-women's sex organs <i>don't</i> matter.<br /> <br /> Vysha is probably correct that the ideal solution would be for the trans community to come up with new words that have the definitions that they want (people are always making up new words) rather than trying to repurpose older words that have had different meanings and get upset at people who don't really understand how the old words are problematic in light of new definitions.<br /> <br /> New words would likely offer a bit less confusion than old ones, though admittedly you're going to run into jerks who refuse to use the new ones (and, of course, getting millions or even billions of people to agree on the meaning of new words can be difficult). But at least then you'd have a good idea of who is being an intentional jackass rather than not knowing if someone is really a jerk or just genuinely ignorant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 01-24-2017, 06:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T14:45:53-08:00","id":1037427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vysha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1037413#post1037413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose the real issue from my perspective is when I get yelled at or harassed for not knowing the proper pronoun to use when talking about or to a specific individual.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just use they/them until told otherwise. Hell, the newest National Geography said to do this, and it finally got my boyfriend's grandmother to stop misgendering him after three years of nonsense. They/them is always an option, and nobody reasonable should get upset for you using it.<br /> <br /> Now, if you keep misgendering someone after they've corrected you? Then you're going to get scolded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T15:10:14-08:00","id":1037436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vysha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1037413#post1037413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, this is where I usually get hung up. I honestly feel like I need to learn a new language when discussing trans issues, which comes up rather often in my work (work at a homeless shelter). And that's alright, it's something I know I'm not familiar with in the least and have a lot to learn about before I can comfortably speak on the subject. I suppose the real issue from my perspective is when I get yelled at or harassed for not knowing the proper pronoun to use when talking about or to a specific individual. It's a new topic for me; I need time to learn. And in all fairness, the trans people are (generally speaking, of course) the ones who are understanding and willing to walk me through the new terminology. It's usually the non-trans people trying to be their advocates who lose their ever-loving mind because I said &amp;quot;male&amp;quot; instead of &amp;quot;man&amp;quot; or something along those lines.<br /> <br /> Sorry, mini-rant over.<br /> <br /> <br /> Omega, we get it. You don't like feminists. Maybe instead of randomly posting about it in a thread about the women's march and related topics, you can start your own anti-feminist thread, where you can explain the many and varied reasons for your hate.</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't hate feminists, don't confuse being critical for hate, because I have a lot of compassion for feminists, I used to be one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T15:16:43-08:00","id":1037440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1037427#post1037427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just use they/them until told otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uhg, I wish it was that simple. And with nearly all the trans-people I've met in my line of work, it usually is. Hell, even the one who got upset that I was &quot;de-gendering them&quot; with gender-neutral pronouns was understanding when I explained it wasn't something intentional, just a vocabulary I was unfamiliar with and still learning (and really, her reaction came from years at a different shelter where the staff was pretty douchy about all things non-hetero). Mostly it's the non-trans who want to pick fights claiming they're protecting others.<br /> <br /> Anyway, it's a side-rant and I don't want to derail things. Sorry about that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T16:14:14-08:00","id":1037461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1037436#post1037436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't hate feminists, don't confuse being critical for hate, because I have a lot of compassion for feminists, I used to be one.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's your responsibility to present your posts in a fashion that doesn't give the impression of you hating feminists/feminism. If a lot of people see you as a hater... it might be because that's just how you keep posting regardless of what's in your heart.<br /> <br /> Also the, &quot;I used to be one,&quot; thing doesn't really help.<br /> <br /> If someone said to you, &quot;RPGs promote devil worship, I should know, I used to play RPGs.&quot; are you going to say, &quot;Wow, maybe RPGs really are the tool of the devil, this guy admitted to playing RPGs!&quot; or are you going to dismiss that aspect of the comment and focus on the actual claim at hand (and probably have a lot of skepticism about their claims to authority on the subject)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T17:02:50-08:00","id":1037488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vysha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1037440#post1037440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uhg, I wish it was that simple. And with nearly all the trans-people I've met in my line of work, it usually is. Hell, even the one who got upset that I was &quot;de-gendering them&quot; with gender-neutral pronouns was understanding when I explained it wasn't something intentional, just a vocabulary I was unfamiliar with and still learning (and really, her reaction came from years at a different shelter where the staff was pretty douchy about all things non-hetero). Mostly it's the non-trans who want to pick fights claiming they're protecting others.<br /> <br /> Anyway, it's a side-rant and I don't want to derail things. Sorry about that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. Don't use &quot;they/them&quot; by default. Use &quot;Excuse me, may I ask what pronouns you prefer?&quot; by default.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T17:11:37-08:00","id":1037494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1037461#post1037461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's your responsibility to present your posts in a fashion that doesn't give the impression of you hating feminists/feminism. If a lot of people see you as a hater... it might be because that's just how you keep posting regardless of what's in your heart.<br /> <br /> Also the, &quot;I used to be one,&quot; thing doesn't really help.<br /> <br /> If someone said to you, &quot;RPGs promote devil worship, I should know, I used to play RPGs.&quot; are you going to say, &quot;Wow, maybe RPGs really are the tool of the devil, this guy admitted to playing RPGs!&quot; or are you going to dismiss that aspect of the comment and focus on the actual claim at hand (and probably have a lot of skepticism about their claims to authority on the subject)?</div> </div> </div> </div>^All of this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T17:12:48-08:00","id":1037495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vysha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1037413#post1037413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Omega, we get it. You don't like feminists. Maybe instead of randomly posting about it in a thread about the women's march and related topics, you can start your own anti-feminist thread, where you can explain the many and varied reasons for your hate.</div> </div> </div> </div>He did. It got deleted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T17:55:09-08:00","id":1037516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1037495#post1037495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He did. It got deleted.</div> </div> </div> </div> I thought I was losing my mind, I went looking for it after a mod said take the discussion to the MRA thread, only to not be able to find it. I'm guessing a different mod deleted it so the mod asking me to move MRA discussion to that thread didn't know it was gone. <br /> <br /> Anyways I've tried to keep my points focused on feminism, the women's March, and related protest movements like BLM. <br /> <br /> And yes I have been critical of the women's March, but not unjustly so. I have tried to be even handed, admitting they had legitimate issues with Trump, admitting they had good reason to be concerned about what he would try and, get judges who would over turn Roe vs. Wade, that cuts to funding for protecting women from violence against women was wrong, ect... <br /> <br /> But having a speaker who murdered, raped, and tortured a man and who appears to say little remorse for it and acts like she is, the real victim, who then gets applauses is disturbing to me, and yet no one seems to care about that, I don't understand it.<br /> <br /> And that a male feminist hit a female journalist who was none violent and no one cared seems like a contradiction to the stated goals of the event, it's illogical, it behavior based on the an ingroup biase that violates the stated principles of the event. <br /> <br /> Logically nothing I have said has been hateful, merely critical, and I have reasonable concerns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T18:03:14-08:00","id":1037524,"title":"","content":"Sure, sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T19:12:44-08:00","id":1037568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1037516#post1037516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But having a speaker who murdered, raped, and tortured a man and who appears to say little remorse for it and acts like she is, the real victim, who then gets applauses is disturbing to me, and yet no one seems to care about that, I don't understand it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because one speaker doesn't represent everyone on a worldwide march. And more realistically most people probably didn't know who she was. You seem to get this when it's about yourself, you claimed in the other thread that you don't share the beliefs of all the other MRA members. But when it comes to groups you disagree with you act like they're a hive mind.<br /> <br /> You're talking about Cherno Biko, right? Because while I see that she's confessed rapist there's nothing about her being a torturer or murderer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T19:48:04-08:00","id":1037597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1037568#post1037568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because one speaker doesn't represent everyone on a worldwide march. And more realistically most people probably didn't know who she was. You seem to get this when it's about yourself, you claimed in the other thread that you don't share the beliefs of all the other MRA members. But when it comes to groups you disagree with you act like they're a hive mind.<br /> <br /> You're talking about Cherno Biko, right? Because while I see that she's confessed rapist there's nothing about her being a torturer or murderer.</div> </div> </div> </div> I absolutely agree that it doesn't represent everyone at the March, I never said it did, but you surely someone can acknowledge what she did was wrong and that it was a bad call to have her as a speaker. <br /> <br /> That no one seems to care is far worse then actually having her as a speaker, people can make mistakes, a simple acknowledgement that doing so was in poor taste and a slap to the face of the GLBT community, not to mention his family is in order. The organizers should apologize, refusing to do so just gives your critics ammunition, and many are not as forgiving or understanding as I am, they have no interest in acknowling that it is not reflective of the whole March as I have, they will use it against the March. <br /> <br /> To ignore the issue does not make it go away, it needs to be confronted, and addressed. <br /> <br /> This wasn't just someone who showed up to the March, the organizers knew what she did and gave her a, position of promence, that's not okay. <br /> <br /> And yes if the MRM rally had a key speaker who did this, I would condemn it too, absolutely, it's the moral thing to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T19:56:54-08:00","id":1037606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.nationalpost.com/m/wp/news/blog.html?b=news.nationalpost.com/full-comment/david-brooks-hope-you-enjoyed-the-womens-march-it-wont-work&amp;pubdate=2017-01-24\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.nationalpost.com/m/wp/news/blog.html?b=news.nationalpost.com/full-comment/david-brooks-hope-you-enjoyed-the-womens-march-it-wont-work&amp;pubdate=2017-01-24\" target=\"_blank\"> 404 Not Found - National Post </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.nationalpost.com/m/wp/news/blog.html?b=news.nationalpost.com/full-comment/david-brooks-hope-you-enjoyed-the-womens-march-it-wont-work&amp;pubdate=2017-01-24\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.nationalpost.com/m/wp/news/blog.html?b=news.nationalpost.com/full-comment/david-brooks-hope-you-enjoyed-the-womens-march-it-wont-work&amp;pubdate=2017-01-24 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> A reality check.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T20:31:08-08:00","id":1037629,"title":"","content":"Your reality check is... the same thing someone says about every march/protest ever regardless of any actual analysis of what makes for effective marches?<br /> <br /> Have a comedy website do far better at a reality check than David Brooks (you know, the conservative with a fairly bad track record of demonstrating a good understanding of the Democratic base...):<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.cracked.com/blog/things-your-angry-relatives-always-get-wrong-about-protests/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.cracked.com/blog/things-y...bout-protests/</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T22:00:03-08:00","id":1037664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1037629#post1037629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your reality check is... the same thing someone says about every march/protest ever regardless of any actual analysis of what makes for effective marches?<br /> <br /> Have a comedy website do far better at a reality check than David Brooks (you know, the conservative with a fairly bad track record of demonstrating a good understanding of the Democratic base...):<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.cracked.com/blog/things-your-angry-relatives-always-get-wrong-about-protests/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.cracked.com/blog/things-y...bout-protests/</a></div> </div> </div> </div> I never said Protest never work, some of course do, I just don't think the women's March will, it wasn't well designed, it wasn't well targeted.<br /> <br /> I think the Occupty protests worked, to a limited degree in one area, it brought to into the public discussion the issue wealth inequality and the fact that the working class has been back sliding. <br /> <br /> But look at the major issues that the Women's March bring, they are already major discussed issues. <br /> <br /> Other protests seek to put pressure on politicians who have a reason to listen, like enviromental protests in places where politicians can score points from backing the protesters. <br /> <br /> But the politicians who would be best moved by the March are already there on things like abortion, the ones that threat it and have the power to back that up are going to be unmoved. <br /> <br /> You have to ask who is going to be moved into action by the protest and what kind of actions are they going to take.<br /> <br /> This event was an all you can eat even for critics, it moved no politicians it needed to, it boosted the fortunes of the ones it needed to. <br /> <br /> Protests can be an asset when used right, but what did this, protest achieve that previous protests didn't already? <br /> <br /> You know what would have made a difference, if those women organized to take out the corrupt insiders within the democractic party, demand the some resignations, not that could have worked, because that would be dealing with fertile ground. <br /> <br /> You know what else could have been useful, lobbying democract officials to filibuster Trump's Supreme Court nominee until he makes a reasonable choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T02:03:37-08:00","id":1037714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1037664#post1037664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never said Protest never work...</div> </div> </div> </div>I never said you said that. I said that Cracked blog piece is a way better reality check than David Brook's piece.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Protests can be an asset when used right, but what did this, protest achieve that previous protests didn't already? </div> </div> </div>Because... as we all know, all protest achievements happen within a week. Did all those &quot;good&quot; protests you consider successful achieve everything in less than a week?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You know what would have made a difference, if those women organized to take out the corrupt insiders within the democractic party, demand the some resignations, not that could have worked, because that would be dealing with fertile ground. </div> </div> </div>Ah, so the big problem with the protest has nothing to do with effectiveness. The problem is that these people protested for something you don't care about, and didn't protest for what you want people to protest for.<br /> <br /> Maybe, you know, women around the world care a bit more about the Trump administration having already started to do make like the global gag rule even stronger than Reagan or the Bushes did (though one has to wonder if Pence had something to do with it since this isn't the first time he's decided to screw over AIDs patients and prevention efforts over separate ideological issues). If you don't know what that's about, since Reagan Republican presidents have instituted a rule that US federal aid can't go to organizations that provide or educate on abortion as part of family planning. Trump removed that last part, so work on STI prevention/treatment that previous Republican presidents recognized needed to be able to discuss the risk of transmission to fetuses and that risk's impact on abortion considerations can no longer get US federal aid. A zika virus NGO worker answers a question about if there's a risk to the fetus that might make the woman consider an abortion? Boom that NGO's funding is at risk... because not talking about abortion (literally talking about it, not even providing it) is now more important than preventing diseases; even ones that might pose a significant risk to fetuses if untreated.<br /> <br /> And compared to that... maybe they care a bit less about being a tool for your political agenda.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T05:29:02-08:00","id":1037777,"title":"","content":"I was talking about Donna Hylton not Cherno Biko, I've never heard of Cherno Biko, holy shit how many sex offenders did they show off at this March?!?<br /> <br /> was Karla Homoka unavailable to make an appearance?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T06:00:43-08:00","id":1037790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1037777#post1037777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was talking about Donna Hylton not Cherno Biko, I've never heard of Cherno Biko, holy shit how many sex offenders did they show off at this March?!?<br 