orting reports from elsewhere. Do you have any other sources supporting your accusation?<br /> <br /> Cherno Biko is <a href=\"http://&quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.womensmarch.com/speakers/&quot;]not</a> listed[/URL] among the Speakers for the women's march. I don't know what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> is talking about.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm relieved to hear that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 01-25-2017, 09:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T06:39:17-08:00","id":1037802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vysha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1037794#post1037794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Much as I hate to support anything MegaPhallic has to say, <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.psychologytoday.com/articles/199507/crime-and-punishment&amp;quot;]here's</a> proof of Donna Hylton's criminal record[/URL].</div> </div> </div> </div> Thanks for finding the link. <br /> <br /> As for Megaphallic, that had me laughing, you actually made my handle sound dirtier.<br /> <br /> Omegaphallic was inspired by Communist Supervillian Omega Red.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T06:39:44-08:00","id":1037803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vysha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1037794#post1037794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Much as I hate to support anything MegaPhallic has to say, <a href=\"https://www.psychologytoday.com/articles/199507/crime-and-punishment\" target=\"_blank\">here's proof of Donna Hylton's criminal record</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming that article is credible and it refers to the same person... (The NYTimes article it references actually spells out name Donna HILton <a href=\"http://www.nytimes.com/1985/04/08/nyregion/the-city-7-held-in-slaying-of-man-in-trunk.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.nytimes.com/1985/04/08/ny...-in-trunk.html</a> )... the situation was a lot more complicated than &quot;Donna Hylton tortured and murderd a man for yuks.&quot; After which, she served her time, and apparently has not shown signs of recidivism. <br /> <br /> Do you believe in &quot;Once a jailbird, always a jailbird?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T06:52:42-08:00","id":1037809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1037803#post1037803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assuming that article is credible and it refers to the same person... (The NYTimes article it references actually spells out name Donna HILton <a href=\"http://www.nytimes.com/1985/04/08/nyregion/the-city-7-held-in-slaying-of-man-in-trunk.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.nytimes.com/1985/04/08/ny...-in-trunk.html</a> )... the situation was a lot more complicated than &amp;quot;Donna Hylton tortured and murderd a man for yuks.&amp;quot; After which, she served her time, and apparently has not shown signs of recidivism. <br /> <br /> Do you believe in &amp;quot;Once a jailbird, always a jailbird?&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> No, I support rehabilitation, I believe she has the right to rebuild her life, but it does make her an inapproitate choice to have a speaker. <br /> <br /> And I don't like that she seems to see herself as the victim, showing no remorse for the absolutely pure fucking evil thing she did. <br /> <br /> Let's be honest if she was a man she'd have gotten life in prison or the death penalty and she would have deserved it (I don't support the death penalty, so I'm talking more about her deserving a life sentence). <br /> <br /> It wasn't just murder, it was that it was just about the most vile murder you can image, rape, torture, and a hate crime as well. <br /> <br /> She has done her time, so I don't support tormenting her, but she does NOT deserve to be treated like a hero.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T07:28:55-08:00","id":1037829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1037809#post1037809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">She has done her time, so I don't support tormenting her, but she does NOT deserve to be treated like a hero.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think percieved heroism has anything to do with it. Most of the time, people just cheer because they support whatever you're saying or doing <i>at that moment</i>, often without regard for history. <br /> <br /> People invest their dreams in the strangest vessels. Our most recent election shows as much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T08:05:16-08:00","id":1037843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1037809#post1037809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I support rehabilitation, I believe she has the right to rebuild her life, but it does make her an inapproitate choice to have a speaker.<br /> <br /> And I don't like that she seems to see herself as the victim, showing no remorse for the absolutely pure fucking evil thing she did.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWould it help if she said it was just guy talk and everybody does it? She's aparently been speaking about mass incarceration, recidivism and women who've been the victims of abuse for years now. Considering her own past she probably knows more than anyone else. You were willing to put aside your criticisms for others, like one of your favorite MRA speakers who threatened to rape someone:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/987143-i-am-done-with-every-us-politician-i-am-voting-elmo-for-potus?p=989106#post989106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But he did apologize, including to the person who he said it to and has since fundraised hundreds of thousands dollars for little girls third world to help them. So I think he's done his pence and his jack assery does nothing to change the points he made in the video. His arguements stand on its own merits.<br /> [You had a video link here]<br /> I do understand why you were horrified by what he said, I just believe as horrible as his actions were he deserves forgiveness, and that many of his points still value, even if I even find him jarring and abrasive at times.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Let's be honest if she was a man she'd have gotten life in prison or the death penalty and she would have deserved it (I don't support the death penalty, so I'm talking more about her deserving a life sentence). </div> </div> </div>Not likely life, even admitted murderers who were the primary actors and had no extenuating circumstances have been released after a decade or two. And New York hasn't executed anyone since 1963.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> She has done her time, so I don't support tormenting her, but she does NOT deserve to be treated like a hero. </div> </div> </div>She's not. She was treated like a speaker, bringing attention to the problems of female victims of abuse and women in the criminal justice system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T11:42:14-08:00","id":1037941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1037843#post1037843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bWould it help if she said it was just guy talk and everybody does it? She's aparently been speaking about mass incarceration, recidivism and women who've been the victims of abuse for years now. Considering her own past she probably knows more than anyone else. You were willing to put aside your criticisms for others, like one of your favorite MRA speakers who threatened to rape someone:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Not likely life, even admitted murderers who were the primary actors and had no extenuating circumstances have been released after a decade or two. And New York hasn't executed anyone since 1963.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> She's not. She was treated like a speaker, bringing attention to the problems of female victims of abuse and women in the criminal justice system.</div> </div> </div> </div> Are you seriously comparing some who was convicted of murder and torture to a couple of guys joking on a bus? <br /> <br /> That is an utter false equivelancy, even if Trump of which there is still no proof of, grabbed some women by the groin, it would still not as serious a crime as raping, torturing, and killing someone, any more then punching someone in the face is the same as cutting there head off. They are not even in the same league. <br /> <br /> They couldn't find a convicted pot dealer to talk about how women are treated in prison?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T11:45:23-08:00","id":1037943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1037809#post1037809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's be honest if she was a man she'd have gotten life in prison or the death penalty and she would have deserved it (I don't support the death penalty, so I'm talking more about her deserving a life sentence).</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, depending on the state you're in... 25 years <i><b>is</b></i> a life sentence. &quot;25 to life&quot; is the specific sentence, I believe. It takes into account that a person can change their ways in prison. And yes, it's given to men as well. This kind of sentence is more often given to younger perpetrators (which she was). And, as mentioned, no man would have been sentenced to death in the state of New York because they stopped giving that sentence. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zacarias_Moussaoui\" target=\"_blank\">Even the guy convicted of aiding the 9-11 hijackers didn't get a death sentence</a>, so it's hard to believe that anyone else would barring radical changes to their criminal justice system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T12:01:23-08:00","id":1037952,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2241\" data-vbnamecard=\"2241\">Omegaphallic</a><br /> <br /> I'm sorry that you are unhappy with the Woman's March. I'm sorry you believe the Woman's March is a waste of time and they should be focusing what you believe are more important issues.<br /> <br /> Yes, I am unhappy one speaker at the march is a convicted murderer. But you know what? I'm still going to support the Woman's March. No, they are not perfect. It is an organization of humans. But I believe in their causes. I'm personally affected by the issues they are fighting for. You searching though the internet for evidence to discredit the march isn't going to change my beliefs. Heck, 99% of arguments on the internet never change anyone's beliefs.<br /> <br /> I do not support murderers and do not believe my support of the Woman's march means I support murderers. Just like I do not believe voting Republican automatically means you disapprove of Gay Rights. To me a person's actions mean more than pressing a button in a poll booth. Unfortunately, it isn't possible to create a custom organization or person that will perfectly represents one's believes. Life is complicated. There is usually not one true answer to any situation. You have to make compromises to achieve any meaningful impact. You have to make the best choices you can, accept your own mistakes and the imperfection of others, and life your life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 01-25-2017, 03:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T12:18:39-08:00","id":1037970,"title":"","content":"In other news, there is a <a href=\"http://gizmodo.com/why-scientists-are-planning-their-own-march-on-washingt-1791618754\" target=\"_blank\">March for Science</a> in the planning stages. Depending on the date, location, and my plans, I may attend this one. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T12:28:52-08:00","id":1037980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1037970#post1037970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In other news, there is a <a href=\"http://gizmodo.com/why-scientists-are-planning-their-own-march-on-washingt-1791618754\" target=\"_blank\">March for Science</a> in the planning stages. Depending on the date, location, and my plans, I may attend this one. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>In before: &quot;They will never accomplish anything with their march!!&quot; &quot;What about faith??&quot; &quot;One of their speakers was convicted of plagiarism and therefore the entire march is plagiarized!!&quot; And my all-time favorite &quot;I don't hate science, I love science, but I stopped being a scientist after they said the Earth was round and now those filthy scientists can die in the fiery pits of Hell.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T12:39:41-08:00","id":1037988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1037952#post1037952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2241\" data-vbnamecard=\"2241\">Omegaphallic</a><br /> <br /> I'm sorry that you are unhappy with the Woman's March. I'm sorry you believe the Woman's March is a waste of time and they should be focusing what you believe are more important issues.<br /> <br /> Yes, I am unhappy one speaker at the march is a convicted murderer. But you know what? I'm still going to support the Woman's March. No, they are not perfect. It is an organization of humans. But I believe in their causes. I'm personally affected by the issues they are fighting for. You searching though the internet for evidence to discredit the march isn't going to change my beliefs. Heck, 99% of arguments on the internet never change anyone's beliefs.<br /> <br /> I do not support murderers and do not believe my support of the Woman's march means I support murderers. Just like I do not believe voting Republican automatically means you disapprove of Gay Rights. To me a person's actions mean more than pressing a button in a poll booth. Unfortunately, it isn't possible to create a custom organization or person that will perfectly represents one's believes. Life is complicated. There is usually not one true answer to any situation. You have to make compromises to achieve any meaningful impact. You have to make the best choices you can, accept your own mistakes and the imperfection of others, and life your life.</div> </div> </div> </div> Okay, I can respect that, you made you point well,, thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 01-25-2017, 03:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T12:48:33-08:00","id":1037989,"title":"","content":"Actually given one of the things that the science March is protesting is being gagged, and the fact that people likely to be less aware of this then the issues of the Women's March, so I can see more use and value in the science March IMO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T12:56:20-08:00","id":1037995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1037941#post1037941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you seriously comparing some who was convicted of murder and torture to a couple of guys joking on a bus?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not comparing the severity of the crime. I'm pointing out what you called your ability to forgive. One person threatened to rape another and apologized and you can look past it because 'many of his points still value.' Another person was an accessory to murder and spent twenty seven years in prison but for you, her mere presence as a speaker talking about her experiences invalidates the entire march. How can you support rehabilitation if you forever associate a person's name with the crime they were punished and rehabilitated for?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That is an utter false equivelancy, even if Trump of which there is still no proof of, grabbed some women by the groin, it would still not as serious a crime as raping, torturing, and killing someone, any more then punching someone in the face is the same as cutting there head off. They are not even in the same league. </div> </div> </div>Either was their punishment or rehabilitation. You shrug off Trump's talk of rape and assault but he was elected president. Another spent over two decades in jail and you think she can't talk about her experiences?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They couldn't find a convicted pot dealer to talk about how women are treated in prison? </div> </div> </div>Donna Hylton seems to have turned her life around and spends her time trying to help get jobs for ex-convicts. There probably are convicted pot dealers who talk about how women are treated in prison. But Donna Hylton is just as experienced as they are, if not more due to her time spent, and can speak personally about the abuse of her childhood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T13:59:55-08:00","id":1038031,"title":"","content":"The best speaker I ever heard on the subject of socially combating Neo-Nazi recruitment was an ex-con that went to prison for kidnapping and torturing someone.<br /> <br /> Does recommending him as a speaker mean I condone his crimes? No, because that's stupid. The reason he's so effective in his anti-Neo-Nazi programs is because he's an ex-Neo-Nazi recruiter which is what lead him to such an atrocious act of violence in the first place. Having been in a super-max facility is a huge part of his story and how it eventually shaped his life outside of prison.<br /> <br /> Are there ex-Neo-Nazis out there that can probably speak eloquently about a lot of the same topics? Sure. But humans respond well to narratives and his guy has one hell of a story to frame his talks about how Neo-Nazi recruitment efforts work and what breaks through the programming.<br /> <br /> Donna Hylton is considering by plenty of people to be in a similar position. She did horrible things, but now she's trying to use that experience to help others understand and prevent more horrible things in the future.<br /> <br /> If you don't let these people speak, you're creating a bubble away from the important - if harsh - truths they are trying to articulate. You're cutting out the people that know the problem more intimately than most <b>for being part of the problem</b> in the past. You don't find harmless pot dealers that are only in prison because of insane sentencing laws doing the human rights violating 23.5 hr lockdown time that is one of the major issues in prison reform around actual treatment of prisoners instead of sentencing reform. Your pool of people that have done enough solitary or extended high security lockup to classify as torture by UN standards, and can still give a solid speech in public about it later, means dealing with people that got convicted of some bad shit. If you oppose them speaking up, you're just saying it's OK to be silent about torture as long as it happens to bad enough people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T14:37:33-08:00","id":1038045,"title":"","content":"Yeah, one of things that got our local priest in troubles was inviting an aging Rockman to do a series of happenings that would show kids why drugs are bad. His story resonated with the audience a lot, and kids kept coming (guy was speaking out of his personal experience and simply shared them, instead of trying to moralize). Dude almost died due to drugs overdose and was a hopeless junkie for years.<br /> Sadly, priest got into troubles from higher ups for bringing a person with such background to the kids and got catapulted far away as a punishment. Which is sad, because he actually managed to make a connection with the youth; his priest-boss is currently waging a full time war on the kids not understanding why he is less popular than That Guy. <br /> So yeah, what Heavy Arms said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T18:47:14-08:00","id":1038166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/shared?ci=rRB3f5CGkIU\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/shared?ci=rRB3f5CGkIU\" target=\"_blank\"> 404 Not Found </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/shared?ci=rRB3f5CGkIU\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/shared?ci=rRB3f5CGkIU </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It turns out Lauren Southern who was assaulted at the Women's March, might be what Thunderfoot calls bullbaiting, stirring shit up on purpose to pick a fight, then editing the video to make it look one sided so it's like OMG look how violent these feminists are, while pretending she didn't egg them on. <br /> <br /> I share this in the name of transparency and ethics, I don't care if she's an MRA, that's unprincipled conduct and bad journalism, and even though I am an MRA I don't condone it, and I condemn it as manipulative and deceitful, not to mention irresponsibly dangerous as one of these people she provokes may someday deal her a serious injury. <br /> <br /> I should have seen this sooner, Lauren Southern seems to get attacked at every leftwing March, Protest, Rally, etc..., what are the odds of that happening so often. <br /> <br /> That doesn't mean the idiots who take the bait don't deserve to be charged for there actions, but Lauren's own pattern of behavior should go into consideration during sentencing.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/shared?ci=jSrwOuD2_iw\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/shared?ci=jSrwOuD2_iw\" target=\"_blank\"> 404 Not Found </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/shared?ci=jSrwOuD2_iw\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/shared?ci=jSrwOuD2_iw </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Another link.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 01-25-2017, 11:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T20:19:16-08:00","id":1038239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1037995#post1037995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not comparing the severity of the crime. I'm pointing out what you called your ability to forgive. One person threatened to rape another and apologized and you can look past it because 'many of his points still value.' Another person was an accessory to murder and spent twenty seven years in prison but for you, her mere presence as a speaker talking about her experiences invalidates the entire march. How can you support rehabilitation if you forever associate a person's name with the crime they were punished and rehabilitated for?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Either was their punishment or rehabilitation. You shrug off Trump's talk of rape and assault but he was elected president. Another spent over two decades in jail and you think she can't talk about her experiences?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Donna Hylton seems to have turned her life around and spends her time trying to help get jobs for ex-convicts. There probably are convicted pot dealers who talk about how women are treated in prison. But Donna Hylton is just as expthat with nced as they are, if not more due to her time spent, and can speak personally about the abuse of her childhood.</div> </div> </div> </div> I support rehabilitation and forgiveness, but there is a difference between forgiving her and making her your poster spokesmen and not bothering to acknowledge the severity of what she did. <br /> <br /> Again if MRA did that, we'd be crucified for it by everyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T00:22:28-08:00","id":1038297,"title":"","content":"Well, she wasn't the &quot;poster spokesman&quot; of the march, and the official march literature did not shy away from her being convicted criminal. It could have been &quot;harsher&quot; in its wording, but to what point? She's a prison reformer activist... who's qualifications are, &quot;was in prison.&quot; What point would there to be trying to litigate the specifics of her crime, when she's not there to talk about her crime anyway?<br /> <br /> Of course, from what little reliable sources are readily available (keeping in mind this was a crime committed in 1985), while the police felt her confession was probably more self-serving than the exact truth, they were also pretty sure she (and the two other women who were initially hired as bait) were not the primary actors in the majority of the torture and sexual assault, and had no direct participation in the murder... so we don't really know the severity of what she personally did. We know the severity of the crime, and we know she willing went along with the plan despite of what it entailed.<br /> <br /> So even if they had detailed some of these things, the Reddit crowd that's reporting the severity of her specific actions in far excess of what the evidence we have suggests. So it wouldn't have shut any of them up, they'd continue to complain that her crimes were being white-washed/etc. Why bother engaging with a fight that you can't win, because the other side only really cares about trying to detract from the value of your protest, and doesn't give a shit about the truth (no matter what their claims are)?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T05:31:42-08:00","id":1038357,"title":"","content":"I honestly don't know, but you could have avoided it all by not inviting her, she can't be the only prison reform activist and honestly given men have it worse on this issue by a vast margin, you could have considered someone who works to reform not just the female prisons, someone who committed a less sever crime like robbery or pot dealing, ect... <br /> <br /> Anyways this wasn't my March just giving some friendly advise for the future, hind sight is 50/50.<br /> <br /> Good luck in your fight against Trump over abortion and the social safety net, I wish you luck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T06:12:19-08:00","id":1038372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1038357#post1038357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I honestly don't know, but you could have avoided it all by not inviting her, she can't be the only prison reform activist and honestly given men have it worse on this issue by a vast margin, you could have considered someone who works to reform not just the female prisons, someone who committed a less sever crime like robbery or pot dealing, ect...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. We should have made the Women's March about Reforming Mens' Prisons. Silly us.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T06:19:16-08:00","id":1038373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1038357#post1038357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I honestly don't know, but you could have avoided it all by not inviting her, she can't be the only prison reform activist and honestly given men have it worse on this issue by a vast margin, you could have considered someone who works to reform not just the female prisons, someone who committed a less sever crime like robbery or pot dealing, ect...</div> </div> </div> </div>Again though, someone who committed a less severe crime isn't likely to be as familiar with the issues with the prison system. As Heavy Arms said on just the last page,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1038031#post1038031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you don't let these people speak, you're creating a bubble away from the important - if harsh - truths they are trying to articulate. You're cutting out the people that know the problem more intimately than most <b>for being part of the problem</b> in the past. You don't find harmless pot dealers that are only in prison because of insane sentencing laws doing the human rights violating 23.5 hr lockdown time that is one of the major issues in prison reform around actual treatment of prisoners instead of sentencing reform. Your pool of people that have done enough solitary or extended high security lockup to classify as torture by UN standards, and can still give a solid speech in public about it later, means dealing with people that got convicted of some bad shit. If you oppose them speaking up, you're just saying it's OK to be silent about torture as long as it happens to bad enough people.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T12:45:46-08:00","id":1038529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1038357#post1038357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I honestly don't know, but you could have avoided it all by not inviting her,</div> </div> </div> </div>Given as - as far as I'm aware - nobody commenting here was involved in that decision making process, what's the point of saying that?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...she can't be the only prison reform activist and honestly given men have it worse on this issue by a vast margin, you could have considered someone who works to reform not just the female prisons,... </div> </div> </div>If you think that men have it worse in US prison systems... you should probably listen to people like Hylton instead of dismissing her for her gender (since if you're aware of how bad it is for men, you clearly have listened to some utter scumbags - even if indirectly - that are men and the crimes involved aren't the problem).<br /> <br /> And they did select someone who works to reform not just female prisons. Hylton's specific story is about a prison that has both male and female inmates... and has such a bad reputation that the last warden is currently an inmate there.<br /> <br /> Your trained reaction to assume that a woman talking about prison system reform only cares about women in prisons is one of those things that makes people think that &quot;MRA = sexist&quot; because... that assumption is sexist.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...someone who committed a less sever crime like robbery or pot dealing, ect... </div> </div> </div>Got ninjaed on the fact that I already addressed this!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T09:38:01-08:00","id":1038944,"title":"","content":"THere's a reason I assume that Phallic is never going to converse in good faith in these conversations and why I think he is only worthy of ridicule as far as it goes here, and this here is it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T12:06:08-08:00","id":1039029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1031175-the-women-s-march-on-washington?p=1038357#post1038357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I honestly don't know, but you could have avoided it all by not inviting her</div> </div> </div> </div>I know. I meant it as a joke, you know? When I personally sent her the invitation, who'd've thought she would actually accept it? I was as shocked as you were. I swear, the next time I'm left in charge of invitations to a protest, I'll run the list by you first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T12:25:34-08:00","id":1039548,"title":"","content":"I have been conversing in good faith. Still clearly my line of inquiry and concern isn't resonating with anyone here I don't think there is anything more I can add to this conversation so I'll move onto other threads that I feel are more productive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/me